and all the black books
are being opened.

263
00:20:21,762 --> 00:20:25,682
We can't support a weapon
that targets our own citizens.

264
00:20:25,850 --> 00:20:27,475
If these mutants,
as you describe...

265
00:20:28,018 --> 00:20:29,978
are already
living among us...

266
00:20:30,146 --> 00:20:31,980
then they are living
here peacefully.

267
00:20:32,148 --> 00:20:33,732
PARKER: We haven't had an
incident in over 10 years.

268
00:20:33,816 --> 00:20:35,150
After what happened
in Cuba?

269
00:20:35,276 --> 00:20:36,609
PARKER: That was
never confirmed.

270
00:20:36,777 --> 00:20:38,987
We have very real
enemies out there...

271
00:20:39,155 --> 00:20:40,488
the Russians, the Chinese.

272
00:20:40,573 --> 00:20:43,658
We are talking about
a tenth of a tenth...

273
00:20:43,826 --> 00:20:45,869
of a tenth
of our population.

274
00:20:46,036 --> 00:20:48,371
Allow me to read
something to you.

275
00:20:48,456 --> 00:20:49,581
Please.

276
00:20:49,665 --> 00:20:52,542
This was acquired by
our friends at the CIA.

277
00:20:52,710 --> 00:20:53,960
It's a dissertation...

278
00:20:54,044 --> 00:20:57,797
written by a mutant
at Oxford University.

279
00:20:58,591 --> 00:20:59,966
And I quote...

280
00:21:00,426 --> 00:21:02,302
"To Homo Neanderthalensis...

281
00:21:02,470 --> 00:21:04,679
"his mutant cousin,
Homo Sapiens... "

282
00:21:05,139 --> 00:21:06,473
which is us...

283
00:21:06,640 --> 00:21:08,641
"was an aberration.

284
00:21:08,809 --> 00:21:11,936
"The arrival of the mutated
human species, Homo Sapiens...

285
00:21:12,104 --> 00:21:16,441
"was followed by the immediate
extinction of their less evolved kin. "

286
00:21:17,067 --> 00:21:18,067
Well...

287
00:21:18,652 --> 00:21:23,072
Now, we are
the Neanderthal.

288
00:21:23,240 --> 00:21:24,991
Speak for yourself,
Dr. Trask.

289
00:21:25,075 --> 00:21:26,618
(ALL LAUGH ING)
(CH UCKLES)

290
00:21:27,161 --> 00:21:29,871
You know, when you sent
our soldiers to Vietnam...

291
00:21:30,039 --> 00:21:31,664
without the weapons they
needed to win the war...

292
00:21:31,832 --> 00:21:33,750
you underestimated
your enemy.

293
00:21:33,876 --> 00:21:37,212
(CH UCKLING) You do that
with this enemy...

294
00:21:37,296 --> 00:21:38,463
Mmm...

295
00:21:38,547 --> 00:21:41,549
and it won't be some border
skirmish halfway around the world.

296
00:21:41,717 --> 00:21:43,885
This time, the war will
be for our streets...

297
00:21:44,053 --> 00:21:46,262
our cities, our homes...

298
00:21:46,430 --> 00:21:50,475
and by the time you see
the need for my program...

299
00:21:50,810 --> 00:21:52,936
it will be too late...

300
00:21:53,103 --> 00:21:57,732
and you will have lost
two wars in one lifetime.

301
00:22:00,653 --> 00:22:02,779
We are sorry,
Dr. Trask...

302
00:22:03,197 --> 00:22:05,532
but your
Sentinel Program...

303
00:22:06,158 --> 00:22:08,159
it ain't gonna fly.

304
00:22:08,410 --> 00:22:10,245
(H ELICOPTER BLADES WH IRRING)

305
00:22:20,756 --> 00:22:21,923
Can I help you, Colonel?

306
00:22:22,007 --> 00:22:24,300
Just here to give our
boys a proper send-off.

307
00:22:24,426 --> 00:22:27,762
I'm sorry, sir, but we have
orders. This is a quarantined area.

308
00:22:27,930 --> 00:22:29,931
Stand aside, soldier.

309
00:22:30,099 --> 00:22:31,975
That's an order.

310
00:22:41,110 --> 00:22:42,110
SOLDIER: Atten-hut!

311
00:22:43,112 --> 00:22:44,195
At ease.
(CLEARS TH ROAT)

312
00:23:07,636 --> 00:23:08,887
What is all this?

313
00:23:08,971 --> 00:23:10,555
Lab reports,
blood tests.

314
00:23:10,973 --> 00:23:12,390
It's all getting packed up
and shipped back.

315
00:23:12,474 --> 00:23:13,600
Where is it going?

316
00:23:13,684 --> 00:23:14,726
Same place they are.

317
00:23:15,519 --> 00:23:16,811
Trask Industries.

318
00:23:18,355 --> 00:23:19,939
STRYKER:
Let's go, gentlemen.

319
00:23:20,024 --> 00:23:22,317
I'm taking you out
of this shit show.

320
00:23:22,484 --> 00:23:24,319
HAVOK: Shipping home?

321
00:23:25,362 --> 00:23:26,529
Not just yet.

322
00:23:27,239 --> 00:23:28,740
What are you doing
with those?

323
00:23:28,824 --> 00:23:30,617
Something to make the ride
a little smoother.

324
00:23:30,868 --> 00:23:33,202
I'm transferring you
to a private facility...

325
00:23:33,829 --> 00:23:35,705
where we can run
a few more tests.

326
00:23:38,751 --> 00:23:39,834
(COLON EL SAN DERS
CLEARS TH ROAT)

327
00:23:41,337 --> 00:23:42,754
Your men
are not military.

328
00:23:44,089 --> 00:23:45,089
Private outfit.

329
00:23:45,549 --> 00:23:47,050
We're authorized
to remand these men.

330
00:23:47,259 --> 00:23:48,259
Hmm.

331
00:23:51,680 --> 00:23:53,431
These troops
are going home.

332
00:23:53,599 --> 00:23:57,602
Well, Colonel, I don't believe you
have jurisdiction in this matter.

333
00:23:58,520 --> 00:24:00,855
I'm afraid I do, son.

334
00:24:01,023 --> 00:24:02,148
I'm sorry, who are you?

335
00:24:02,775 --> 00:24:04,442
The question is,
Major...

336
00:24:08,697 --> 00:24:09,697
...who are you?

337
00:24:12,034 --> 00:24:13,034
(GRU NTS)

338
00:24:15,037 --> 00:24:16,037
(GRU NTS)

339
00:24:16,372 --> 00:24:17,372
(GRU NTS)

340
00:24:18,248 --> 00:24:19,374
(GRU NTS)

341
00:24:22,920 --> 00:24:23,920
(GROANS)

342
00:24:38,060 --> 00:24:39,060
(SCREAMS)

343
00:24:40,729 --> 00:24:41,729
(GRU NTS)

344
00:24:49,989 --> 00:24:51,072
(CHOKING)

345
00:24:55,119 --> 00:24:56,202
Raven!

346
00:24:56,620 --> 00:24:57,996
That's not my name.

347
00:25:01,417 --> 00:25:02,917
(GRU NTING)

348
00:25:03,585 --> 00:25:05,586
(EXHALES SHARPLY)
I had that.

349
00:25:05,754 --> 00:25:06,838
I know.

350
00:25:08,674 --> 00:25:10,633
Let's move out.
Come on, let's go.

351
00:25:10,801 --> 00:25:11,968
HAVOK: Where's Erik?

352
00:25:12,136 --> 00:25:13,219
I'm on my own now.

353
00:25:16,682 --> 00:25:17,974
Let's go! Move it!

354
00:25:18,183 --> 00:25:20,268
(SOLDIERS
YELLING IN DISTINCTLY)

355
00:25:36,744 --> 00:25:38,286
Hold that plane!

356
00:25:38,787 --> 00:25:41,622
Wouldn't wanna leave these boys
in this godforsaken country.

357
00:25:41,790 --> 00:25:42,790
SOLDIER: Yes, sir.

358
00:25:43,459 --> 00:25:45,334
You're not coming
with us, are you?

359
00:25:45,794 --> 00:25:47,170
My war's not over.

360
00:25:47,337 --> 00:25:48,880
The enemy is
still out there.

361
00:26:12,154 --> 00:26:14,072
The four privates,
where did they go?

362
00:26:14,239 --> 00:26:16,074
They were headed
towards the tarmac.

363
00:27:14,842 --> 00:27:16,217
Can I help you?

364
00:27:16,635 --> 00:27:19,095
Uh... Yeah, what happened to the school?

365
00:27:19,263 --> 00:27:22,223
The school's been shut for
years. Are you a parent?

366
00:27:22,307 --> 00:27:25,017
(SCOFFS) I sure as hell
hope not. Who are you?

367
00:27:25,227 --> 00:27:27,228
I'm Hank. Hank McCoy.

368
00:27:27,354 --> 00:27:29,397
I look after the house now.

369
00:27:30,190 --> 00:27:31,440
You're Beast?

370
00:27:31,525 --> 00:27:33,943
Look at you. I guess
you're a late bloomer.

371
00:27:34,069 --> 00:27:35,194
I don't know what
you're talking about,

372
00:27:35,279 --> 00:27:36,863
but I'm gonna have
to ask you to leave.

373
00:27:37,114 --> 00:27:38,698
(GRU NTS)
So where's the Professor?

374
00:27:38,782 --> 00:27:40,032
There's no professor here.

375
00:27:40,117 --> 00:27:42,243
You're pretty strong
for a scrawny kid.

376
00:27:42,411 --> 00:27:44,704
You sure there's not
a little Beast in there?

377
00:27:44,788 --> 00:27:46,497
No, he's not here.
Come on, Beast.

378
00:27:46,582 --> 00:27:48,040
Come on, Beastie.
No.

379
00:27:48,250 --> 00:27:49,876
(GRU NTS) Hey!

380
00:27:51,420 --> 00:27:52,628
I said
the school's closed.

381
00:27:52,754 --> 00:27:54,755
You need to leave. Not
until I see the Professor.

382
00:27:54,923 --> 00:27:57,383
There's no professor here,
I told you that.

383
00:27:57,509 --> 00:28:01,053
Look, kid. You and I are
gonna be good friends.

384
00:28:01,513 --> 00:28:03,222
(GRU NTS)
(GROANS)

385
00:28:03,307 --> 00:28:05,266
You just don't know it yet.

386
00:28:05,684 --> 00:28:07,727
(GROANS)

387
00:28:07,811 --> 00:28:09,312
Professor!

388
00:28:09,938 --> 00:28:11,397
(GROANS)

389
00:28:11,481 --> 00:28:12,481
(GRU NTS)

390
00:28:15,444 --> 00:28:16,652
Professor!

391
00:28:18,030 --> 00:28:19,322
(ROARS)
(GRU NTS)

392
00:28:19,781 --> 00:28:21,115
(HAN K ROARS)

393
00:28:21,450 --> 00:28:23,117
(LOGAN SCREAMING)

394
00:28:24,912 --> 00:28:25,912
(ROARS)

395
00:28:31,710 --> 00:28:33,336
CHARLES: Hank?

396
00:28:33,503 --> 00:28:35,296
What's going on here?

397
00:28:36,632 --> 00:28:37,798
Professor?

398
00:28:37,883 --> 00:28:39,175
Please don't
call me that.

399
00:28:39,301 --> 00:28:40,801
Why?
You know this guy?

400
00:28:40,969 --> 00:28:43,262
Yeah, he looks
slightly familiar.

401
00:28:43,347 --> 00:28:45,556
Get off the bloody
chandelier, Hank.

402
00:28:45,641 --> 00:28:47,350
(GLASS CLIN KING)

403
00:28:47,434 --> 00:28:48,768
You can walk.

404
00:28:48,936 --> 00:28:50,144
You're a perceptive one.

405
00:28:50,270 --> 00:28:51,812
I thought Erik...

406
00:28:51,980 --> 00:28:53,105
Which makes it
slightly perplexing that

407
00:28:53,190 --> 00:28:55,066
you missed our
sign on the way in.

408
00:28:55,150 --> 00:28:56,400
This is private property,
my friend.

409
00:28:56,485 --> 00:28:58,611
I'm gonna have to ask him
to ask you to leave.

410
00:28:58,737 --> 00:29:00,154
Well. (SIGHS)

411
00:29:00,239 --> 00:29:02,156
I'm afraid
I can't do that...

412
00:29:04,534 --> 00:29:06,160
because I was
sent here for you.

413
00:29:06,328 --> 00:29:09,288
Well, tell whoever it was
that sent you that I'm busy.

414
00:29:10,207 --> 00:29:11,499
That's gonna be
a little tricky...

415
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:15,336
because the person
who sent me was you.

416
00:29:15,504 --> 00:29:16,504
What?

417
00:29:16,588 --> 00:29:18,256
About 50 years from now.

418
00:29:18,423 --> 00:29:19,840
Like in the future,
50 years from now?

419
00:29:19,925 --> 00:29:20,925
Yeah.

420
00:29:21,009 --> 00:29:22,927
I sent you from the future?
Yeah.

421
00:29:23,512 --> 00:29:24,637
CHARLES: Piss off.

422
00:29:25,847 --> 00:29:28,432
If you had your powers, you'd
know I was telling the truth.

423
00:29:28,600 --> 00:29:31,227
How do you know
I don't have my p...

424
00:29:31,478 --> 00:29:33,062
Who are you?
LOGAN: I told you.

425
00:29:33,146 --> 00:29:34,605
Are you CIA?
No.

426
00:29:34,690 --> 00:29:35,690
You've been watching me?

427
00:29:35,816 --> 00:29:37,483
I know you, Charles.

428
00:29:37,567 --> 00:29:39,568
We've been friends
for years.

429
00:29:39,945 --> 00:29:41,696
I know your powers
came when you were 9.

430
00:29:42,531 --> 00:29:44,573
I know you thought you were
going crazy when it started...

431
00:29:44,741 --> 00:29:46,784
all the voices
in your head.

432
00:29:46,868 --> 00:29:48,411
And it wasn't
until you were 12...

433
00:29:48,495 --> 00:29:51,998
that you realized all the voices
were in everyone else's head.

434
00:29:52,165 --> 00:29:54,375
Do you want me to go on?

435
00:29:55,544 --> 00:29:57,044
I never told anyone that.

436
00:29:57,129 --> 00:30:00,756
Not yet, no,
but, you will.

437
00:30:02,009 --> 00:30:03,426
All right,
you've piqued my interest.

438
00:30:03,510 --> 00:30:05,094
What do you want?

439
00:30:05,262 --> 00:30:07,346
We have to stop Raven.

440
00:30:09,683 --> 00:30:11,600
I need your help.

441
00:30:12,728 --> 00:30:14,520
We need your help.

442
00:30:18,734 --> 00:30:20,818
I think I'd like
to wake up now.

443
00:30:23,780 --> 00:30:25,114
(SIGHS)

444
00:30:25,907 --> 00:30:27,992
What does she
have to do with this?

445
00:30:32,205 --> 00:30:33,873
CHARLES: So you're saying...

446
00:30:33,957 --> 00:30:36,167
they took Raven's
power, and what?

447
00:30:36,501 --> 00:30:38,711
They weaponized it?

448
00:30:38,879 --> 00:30:39,879
Yep.

449
00:30:40,339 --> 00:30:42,089
She is unique.

450
00:30:42,257 --> 00:30:44,175
Yeah, she is, Hank.

451
00:30:44,343 --> 00:30:47,261
LOGAN: In the beginning, the
Sentinels were just targeting mutants.

452
00:30:47,346 --> 00:30:50,222
Then they began to identify
the genetics in non-mutants...

453
00:30:51,600 --> 00:30:54,977
who would eventually have mutant
children and grandchildren.

454
00:30:55,520 --> 00:30:58,522
Many of the humans tried to
help us, but it was a slaughter.

455
00:30:58,940 --> 00:31:01,692
leaving only the worst
of humanity in charge.

456
00:31:01,860 --> 00:31:03,819
I've been in a lot of wars.

457
00:31:05,947 --> 00:31:07,823
I'd never seen
anything like this.

458
00:31:08,617 --> 00:31:10,117
And it all starts
with her.

459
00:31:10,202 --> 00:31:12,661
Let's just say
for the sake of...

460
00:31:13,663 --> 00:31:16,415
the sake, that I
choose to believe you...

461
00:31:16,583 --> 00:31:19,627
that I choose to help you.
Raven won't listen to me.

462
00:31:20,587 --> 00:31:21,712
(SIGHS)

463
00:31:21,797 --> 00:31:25,716
Her heart and soul
belong to someone else now.

464
00:31:26,134 --> 00:31:27,218
LOGAN: I know.

465
00:31:29,096 --> 00:31:31,722
That's why we're
gonna need Magneto, too.

466
00:31:32,099 --> 00:31:34,100
HAN K: Erik?
(LAUGH ING)

467
00:31:34,643 --> 00:31:36,060
You do know where he is?
Yeah.

468
00:31:37,479 --> 00:31:39,271
(LAUGH ING)

469
00:31:42,609 --> 00:31:43,859
He's where he belongs.

470
00:31:44,945 --> 00:31:46,445
You're just
gonna walk out?

471
00:31:46,530 --> 00:31:49,115
Ooh, top marks. Like I
said, you are perceptive.

472
00:31:49,199 --> 00:31:51,075
The Professor I know would
never turn his back...

473
00:31:51,243 --> 00:31:53,160
on someone who'd
lost their path.

474
00:31:53,328 --> 00:31:55,329
Especially
someone he loved.

475
00:31:57,749 --> 00:31:59,083
You know...

476
00:31:59,251 --> 00:32:01,377
I think I do
remember you now.

477
00:32:01,545 --> 00:32:03,754
Yeah. We came to
you a long time ago...

478
00:32:03,839 --> 00:32:05,965
seeking your help.

479
00:32:06,508 --> 00:32:09,969
And I'm gonna say to you
what you said to us then.

480
00:32:11,721 --> 00:32:12,930
Fuck off.

481
00:32:13,432 --> 00:32:14,723
Listen to me,
you little shit.

482
00:32:15,225 --> 00:32:18,352
I've come a long way, and I've
watched a lot of people die.

483
00:32:18,520 --> 00:32:20,187
Good people. Friends.

484
00:32:20,439 --> 00:32:21,730
If you're gonna
wallow in self-pity...

485
00:32:21,857 --> 00:32:23,691
and do nothing, then you're
gonna watch the same thing...

486
00:32:23,775 --> 00:32:25,443
you understand?

487
00:32:30,198 --> 00:32:32,199
We all have to
die sometime.

488
00:32:37,289 --> 00:32:38,914
Told you there was
no professor here.

489
00:32:41,168 --> 00:32:43,002
What the hell
happened to him?

490
00:32:46,923 --> 00:32:48,924
HANK: He lost everything.

491
00:32:49,092 --> 00:32:51,510
Erik, Raven...

492
00:32:51,678 --> 00:32:53,471
his legs.

493
00:32:53,638 --> 00:32:56,515
(SIGHS) We built the school,
the labs, this whole place...

494
00:32:56,725 --> 00:33:00,436
then, just after
the first semester...

495
00:33:00,604 --> 00:33:02,188
the war in Vietnam
got worse.

496
00:33:03,273 --> 00:33:04,773
Many of the teachers...

497
00:33:05,192 --> 00:33:07,776
and older students
were drafted.

498
00:33:08,153 --> 00:33:09,487
It broke him.

499
00:33:09,946 --> 00:33:12,281
He retreated into himself.

500
00:33:12,449 --> 00:33:14,700
I wanted to help,
do something...

501
00:33:14,868 --> 00:33:16,911
so I designed a serum
to treat his spine...

502
00:33:17,078 --> 00:33:21,123
derived from the same formula
that helps me control my mutation.

503
00:33:22,375 --> 00:33:25,085
(SIGHS) I take just enough
to keep myself balanced...

504
00:33:26,755 --> 00:33:28,214
but he takes too much.

505
00:33:28,632 --> 00:33:30,633
I tried easing him back...

506
00:33:30,800 --> 00:33:34,303
but he just couldn't bear
the pain, the voices.

507
00:33:34,471 --> 00:33:36,931
The treatment
gives him his legs...

508
00:33:37,682 --> 00:33:39,600
but it's not enough.

509
00:33:39,809 --> 00:33:40,809
He's...

510
00:33:43,438 --> 00:33:45,105
He's just lost too much.

511
00:33:47,651 --> 00:33:49,026
(SIGHS)

512
00:33:58,328 --> 00:33:59,954
YOU NG RAVEN: You're
not scared of me?

513
00:34:00,830 --> 00:34:04,041
YOU NG CHARLES: I always believed I
couldn't be the only one in the world.

514
00:34:04,918 --> 00:34:06,085
Charles Xavier.

515
00:34:08,797 --> 00:34:09,964
Raven.

516
00:34:11,341 --> 00:34:13,050
You're hungry and alone.

517
00:34:13,426 --> 00:34:14,885
Take whatever you want.

518
00:34:14,970 --> 00:34:17,888
We've got lots of food.
You don't have to steal.

519
00:34:18,890 --> 00:34:20,099
In fact...

520
00:34:20,267 --> 00:34:22,768
you never have to
steal again.

521
00:34:23,103 --> 00:34:25,104
And that's a promise.

522
00:34:30,652 --> 00:34:32,695
CHARLES: I'll
help you get her.

523
00:34:34,281 --> 00:34:37,575
Not for any of your
future shite, but for her.

524
00:34:37,742 --> 00:34:38,909
Fair enough.

525
00:34:40,078 --> 00:34:42,204
But I'll tell you this.
You don't know Erik.

526
00:34:42,414 --> 00:34:44,999
That man is a monster.
A murderer.

527
00:34:45,125 --> 00:34:47,876
You think you can
convince Raven to change?

528
00:34:47,961 --> 00:34:49,086
To come home?

529
00:34:49,504 --> 00:34:50,921
That's splendid.

530
00:34:51,798 --> 00:34:54,341
But what makes you think
you can change him?

531
00:34:54,509 --> 00:34:58,095
Because you and Erik sent
me back here together.

532
00:35:00,932 --> 00:35:02,433
HAN K: The room
they're holding him in

533
00:35:02,517 --> 00:35:03,809
was built during
the Second World War...

534
00:35:03,977 --> 00:35:05,519
when there was
a shortage of steel.

535
00:35:05,604 --> 00:35:09,440
So the foundation is pure
concrete and sand. No metal.

536
00:35:09,608 --> 00:35:10,691
CHARLES:
He's being held...

537
00:35:10,859 --> 00:35:13,068
a hundred floors
beneath the most

538
00:35:13,194 --> 00:35:15,446
heavily guarded
building on the planet.

539
00:35:15,614 --> 00:35:16,989
LOGAN: Why is he in there?

540
00:35:18,700 --> 00:35:19,950
What, he forgot
to mention?

541
00:35:20,910 --> 00:35:21,910
(SN ICKERING)

542
00:35:22,120 --> 00:35:23,162
Uh, J FK.

543
00:35:23,580 --> 00:35:24,622
He killed...

544
00:35:24,706 --> 00:35:25,873
(CH UCKLING)

545
00:35:25,957 --> 00:35:29,627
What else explains a bullet
miraculously curving through the air?

546
00:35:29,794 --> 00:35:31,420
Erik's always had
a way with guns.

547
00:35:31,546 --> 00:35:33,213
Are you sure you want
to carry on with this?

548
00:35:33,298 --> 00:35:34,673
This is your plan,
not mine.

549
00:35:34,758 --> 00:35:36,842
HAN K: We don't have any
resources to get us in.

550
00:35:36,926 --> 00:35:38,594
CHARLES: Or out.

551
00:35:39,220 --> 00:35:40,846
It's just me and Hank.

552
00:35:41,014 --> 00:35:42,348
I knew a guy.

553
00:35:42,557 --> 00:35:43,974
Yeah, he'd be
a young man now.

554
00:35:44,100 --> 00:35:47,394
Grew up outside of D.C.
(CH UCKLING)

555
00:35:47,520 --> 00:35:49,104
He could get
into anywhere.

556
00:35:49,272 --> 00:35:51,815
I just don't know how the hell
we're gonna find him.

557
00:35:53,151 --> 00:35:55,819
Is Cerebro out
of the question?

558
00:35:58,406 --> 00:36:00,616
We have a phonebook.

559
00:36:06,956 --> 00:36:09,249
I thought you'd be getting
ready for your trip, sir.

560
00:36:09,417 --> 00:36:11,293
I just came to
grab a couple files.

561
00:36:11,461 --> 00:36:14,880
Is that a new scarf?
It's nice.

562
00:36:15,048 --> 00:36:16,131
Thank you.

563
00:37:03,555 --> 00:37:04,555
(BEEPS)

564
00:37:37,547 --> 00:37:38,672
(BREATH TREMBLING)

565
00:37:40,925 --> 00:37:42,009
(GASPS)

566
00:37:47,432 --> 00:37:48,682
Dr. Trask?

567
00:37:48,767 --> 00:37:49,850
One second.

568
00:37:50,935 --> 00:37:52,102
Oh.

569
00:37:52,187 --> 00:37:54,688
We added some names
to the Paris meeting.

570
00:37:58,193 --> 00:37:59,443
Thank you.

571
00:38:00,612 --> 00:38:01,945
Is something wrong, sir?

572
00:38:02,906 --> 00:38:05,032
No. It's nothing.

573
00:38:05,366 --> 00:38:07,951
Would you mind
typing up my itinerary?

574
00:38:08,578 --> 00:38:10,120
I don't wanna
miss anything.

575
00:38:18,421 --> 00:38:19,922
LOGAN: Here, here, here.
CHARLES: Where?

576
00:38:20,006 --> 00:38:21,423
Just stop here.
All right, all right.

577
00:38:21,591 --> 00:38:23,717
Next time I'm driving.
Don't get used to it.

578
00:38:28,848 --> 00:38:29,848
(CAR DOOR CLOSES)

579
00:38:30,809 --> 00:38:31,975
(MAN TALKING ON TV)

580
00:38:41,402 --> 00:38:43,195
(SIGHS)
What's he done now?

581
00:38:43,279 --> 00:38:45,030
I will just write you a
check for whatever he took.

582
00:38:45,198 --> 00:38:46,448
We just need
to talk to him.

583
00:38:48,993 --> 00:38:53,330
Peter! The cops
are here. Again.

584
00:38:53,414 --> 00:38:55,499
(ROCK MUSIC PLAYING)
(PLAYING PING-PONG)

585
00:39:00,380 --> 00:39:01,463
PETER: What do
you guys want?

586
00:39:01,631 --> 00:39:04,299
I didn't do anything.
I've been here all day.

587
00:39:05,426 --> 00:39:07,386
Just relax, Peter.
We're not cops.

588
00:39:07,554 --> 00:39:08,595
Of course you're not.
If you were,

589
00:39:08,680 --> 00:39:09,763
you wouldn't be
driving a rental car.

590
00:39:09,931 --> 00:39:10,931
How did you know
we've got a rental car?

591
00:39:11,057 --> 00:39:12,933
I checked your registration when
you were walking to the door.

592
00:39:13,059 --> 00:39:14,017
I also had
some time to kill

593
00:39:14,102 --> 00:39:15,102
so I went through
your rental agreement.

594
00:39:15,270 --> 00:39:17,354
Saw you were from out
of town. Are you FBl?

595
00:39:18,314 --> 00:39:20,440
No, you're not cops. Hey, what's
with this gifted youngsters place?

596
00:39:20,608 --> 00:39:22,943
That's an old card.

597
00:39:24,195 --> 00:39:26,196
He's fascinating.
He's a pain in the arse.

598
00:39:26,364 --> 00:39:27,531
What, a teleporter?

599
00:39:27,699 --> 00:39:28,782
No, he's just fast.

600
00:39:28,908 --> 00:39:31,326
And when I knew him
he wasn't so... young.

601
00:39:32,161 --> 00:39:33,996
PETER: Young?
You're just old.

602
00:39:34,998 --> 00:39:36,874
So you're not afraid
to show your powers?

603
00:39:37,041 --> 00:39:38,375
What powers? What
are you talking about?

604
00:39:39,377 --> 00:39:40,836
Do you see
something strange here?

605
00:39:42,005 --> 00:39:44,131
Nothing anybody would
believe if you told them.

606
00:39:46,968 --> 00:39:48,176
(ARCADE GAME PINGING)

607
00:39:48,261 --> 00:39:49,803
So, who are you?
What do you want?

608
00:39:49,888 --> 00:39:51,555
LOGAN: We need your
help, Peter. For what?

609
00:39:51,723 --> 00:39:53,765
To break into a highly
secured facility...

610
00:39:54,183 --> 00:39:55,475
and to get someone out.

611
00:39:55,643 --> 00:39:56,685
Prison break?

612
00:39:57,353 --> 00:39:58,520
That's illegal, you know.

613
00:39:58,813 --> 00:39:59,813
Um...

614
00:40:02,901 --> 00:40:04,735
Well, only if
you get caught.

615
00:40:04,903 --> 00:40:05,944
So, what's in it for me?

616
00:40:06,029 --> 00:40:09,406
You, you kleptomaniac, get
to break into the Pentagon.

617
00:40:15,330 --> 00:40:16,997
How do I know
I can trust you?

618
00:40:17,999 --> 00:40:19,499
Because we're
just like you.

619
00:40:21,794 --> 00:40:23,003
Show him.

620
00:40:24,839 --> 00:40:26,340
(BREATH ES DEEPLY)

621
00:40:34,891 --> 00:40:36,850
That's cool,
but it's disgusting.

622
00:40:38,686 --> 00:40:43,482
TOU R GU IDE: Built in 1943, the Pentagon
is the world's largest office building...

623
00:40:43,650 --> 00:40:46,526
housing more than
25,000 military employees...

624
00:40:46,694 --> 00:40:48,278
stretched over six
million square feet.

625
00:40:48,363 --> 00:40:49,363
Where's the bathroom?

626
00:40:49,864 --> 00:40:52,282
GIRL: He always needs
to pee! (ALL LAUGH)

627
00:41:12,053 --> 00:41:14,054
(STATIC CRACKLES)

628
00:41:23,272 --> 00:41:24,773
(DOOR BUZZING)

629
00:41:41,374 --> 00:41:42,624
(ELEVATOR BELL DINGS)

630
00:41:55,263 --> 00:41:57,514
Yeah, we're getting broadcast
signal down here. What's going on?

631
00:41:57,598 --> 00:41:59,433
Damn it, call Maintenance,
get them down here.

632
00:42:10,445 --> 00:42:11,611
(CH UCKLES)

633
00:42:14,574 --> 00:42:15,615
(SHOES SQU EAKING)

634
00:43:09,087 --> 00:43:10,253
(VIBRATING)

635
00:43:20,515 --> 00:43:21,515
(RUMBLING)

636
00:43:32,318 --> 00:43:34,069
(ALARM BLARING)

637
00:43:36,364 --> 00:43:40,158
...fought for and captured the island
of Iwo Jima from the Japanese Empire.

638
00:43:40,827 --> 00:43:42,202
Now, this month-long battle...

639
00:43:42,370 --> 00:43:43,912
included some of
the fiercest fighting

640
00:43:44,038 --> 00:43:45,580
during World War
ll in the Pacific...

641
00:43:45,706 --> 00:43:48,291
(CH EF SPEAKING FRENCH)

642
00:43:48,584 --> 00:43:50,168
(ALARM BLARING)

643
00:43:51,546 --> 00:43:53,964
(GRU NTS)

644
00:44:01,389 --> 00:44:03,723
ERIK: In three seconds, those
doors are going to open...

645
00:44:03,891 --> 00:44:06,226
and 20 guards will
be here to shoot us.

646
00:44:07,270 --> 00:44:09,062
I know. That's what
I'm waiting for.

647
00:44:09,147 --> 00:44:10,230
What are you doing?

648
00:44:10,314 --> 00:44:11,982
I'm holding your neck so
you don't get whiplash.

649
00:44:12,066 --> 00:44:13,066
What?

650
00:44:13,192 --> 00:44:15,402
(SLOWLY) Whiplash.

651
00:44:19,907 --> 00:44:21,241
GUARD: Don't move!

652
00:44:22,076 --> 00:44:23,076
(GRU NTS)

653
00:44:24,245 --> 00:44:25,245
(ALL GROAN)

654
00:44:30,877 --> 00:44:31,877
(EXHALES SHARPLY)

655
00:44:36,257 --> 00:44:37,507
PETER: You're
good, it'll pass.

656
00:44:37,592 --> 00:44:38,758
It happens with everyone.

657
00:44:41,262 --> 00:44:43,430
You must have done
something pretty serious.

658
00:44:43,556 --> 00:44:44,973
What did you do, man?

659
00:44:45,057 --> 00:44:46,558
What did you do?

660
00:44:46,642 --> 00:44:48,351
What did you do? Why'd
they have you in there?

661
00:44:48,436 --> 00:44:50,228
For killing the President.

662
00:44:51,022 --> 00:44:54,191
Ah. Wow.
(WH ISPERS) Shit.

663
00:44:54,984 --> 00:44:56,651
The only thing
I'm guilty of

664
00:44:56,736 --> 00:44:58,320
is fighting for
people like us.

665
00:44:58,487 --> 00:45:00,363
You take karate?
You know karate, man?

666
00:45:00,448 --> 00:45:02,574
I don't know karate.

667
00:45:02,742 --> 00:45:03,992
But I know crazy.

668
00:45:04,076 --> 00:45:05,076
(CH UCKLES)

669
00:45:05,161 --> 00:45:07,996
Ladies and gentlemen, boys and
girls, this is a Code Red situation.

670
00:45:08,080 --> 00:45:10,081
We are evacuating
the entire floor...

671
00:45:10,166 --> 00:45:12,876
so that my associate and I...

672
00:45:12,960 --> 00:45:14,586
can, uh, secure the prison.

673
00:45:14,670 --> 00:45:16,171
Who are you?

674
00:45:16,297 --> 00:45:17,839
We're special operations,
CB...

675
00:45:17,965 --> 00:45:19,257
FB-CID.

676
00:45:19,342 --> 00:45:22,177
Perhaps you didn't hear me
when first I spoke...

677
00:45:22,261 --> 00:45:24,095
but it is imperative
that you understand...

678
00:45:24,180 --> 00:45:25,722
we're in a complete
lockdown situation.

679
00:45:25,806 --> 00:45:27,474
We have to get you
to the third floor...

680
00:45:27,558 --> 00:45:28,892
(GRU NTS)

681
00:45:34,523 --> 00:45:36,566
Oh, I'm sorry.
Were you finished?

682
00:45:38,527 --> 00:45:39,778
(GRU NTING)

683
00:45:41,781 --> 00:45:43,657
They told me
you control metal.

684
00:45:44,033 --> 00:45:45,242
"They"?

685
00:45:46,118 --> 00:45:47,327
(ELEVATOR BELL DINGS)

686
00:45:48,204 --> 00:45:51,414
You know, my mom once knew
a guy who could do that.

687
00:45:54,001 --> 00:45:56,920
I'm sorry, I'm just not
very good with violence.

688
00:45:57,213 --> 00:45:58,797
(ELEVATOR BELL DINGS)

689
00:45:59,799 --> 00:46:01,299
Charles?

690
00:46:01,634 --> 00:46:02,634
(GRU NTS)

691
00:46:03,177 --> 00:46:04,803
(CHARLES GROANS)

692
00:46:08,015 --> 00:46:09,933
Good to see you too,
old friend.

693
00:46:10,101 --> 00:46:11,226
And walking.

694
00:46:11,352 --> 00:46:12,811
No thanks to you.

695
00:46:14,272 --> 00:46:16,731
You're the last person in the
world I expected to see today.

696
00:46:16,899 --> 00:46:18,191
Believe me...

697
00:46:18,359 --> 00:46:20,026
I wouldn't be here
if I didn't have to.

698
00:46:20,361 --> 00:46:22,362
If we get you out of here,
we do it my way.

699
00:46:22,530 --> 00:46:23,530
No killing.

700
00:46:23,948 --> 00:46:24,948
No helmet.

701
00:46:25,574 --> 00:46:27,534
I couldn't disobey
you even if I wanted.

702
00:46:27,702 --> 00:46:30,245
I'm never getting
inside of that head again.

703
00:46:31,580 --> 00:46:33,540
I need your word, Erik.

704
00:46:36,752 --> 00:46:37,877
Nobody move!

705
00:46:38,379 --> 00:46:40,380
Hold it right there!

706
00:46:42,425 --> 00:46:44,092
Charles.
GUARD: Don't move.

707
00:46:44,260 --> 00:46:46,261
Hands up,
or we will shoot!

708
00:46:46,429 --> 00:46:48,054
Freeze them, Charles.
I can't.

709
00:46:48,139 --> 00:46:49,431
Hands up!

710
00:46:52,268 --> 00:46:53,560
(CLATTERING)

711
00:46:54,103 --> 00:46:55,186
No!

712
00:47:05,614 --> 00:47:07,240
(MELLOW '70s SONG PLAYING)

713
00:47:08,075 --> 00:47:12,287
If I could save time
in a bottle

714
00:47:13,581 --> 00:47:18,460
The first thing
that I'd like to do

715
00:47:18,544 --> 00:47:21,171
Is to save every day

716
00:47:21,255 --> 00:47:25,050
Till eternity passes away

717
00:47:25,134 --> 00:47:28,094
Just to spend them with you

718
00:47:29,347 --> 00:47:33,600
If I could make days
last forever

719
00:47:34,685 --> 00:47:38,271
If words could make
wishes come true

720
00:47:39,857 --> 00:47:42,442
I'd save every day

721
00:47:42,526 --> 00:47:45,362
Like a treasure and then

722
00:47:45,446 --> 00:47:49,824
Again,
I would spend them with you

723
00:47:50,534 --> 00:47:53,661
But there never seems
to be enough time

724
00:47:53,746 --> 00:47:56,164
To do the things
you want to do

725
00:47:56,248 --> 00:47:58,917
Once you find them

726
00:48:01,796 --> 00:48:04,130
I've looked around
enough to know

727
00:48:04,215 --> 00:48:08,927
That you're the one I want
to go through time with

728
00:48:22,024 --> 00:48:24,317
(ALL GRU NTING)

729
00:48:28,614 --> 00:48:30,240
(ALARM CONTIN U ES RINGING)

730
00:48:48,509 --> 00:48:50,009
Thanks, kid.

731
00:48:54,682 --> 00:48:56,724
CHARLES: Peter,
thank you very, very much.

732
00:48:56,892 --> 00:48:57,892
You take care.

733
00:48:58,060 --> 00:48:59,310
PETER: Hey, I saw your
flight plan in the cockpit.

734
00:48:59,395 --> 00:49:00,395
Why are you going to Paris?

735
00:49:12,032 --> 00:49:13,783
Imagine if they were metal.

736
00:49:15,202 --> 00:49:16,953
CHARLES: Do me a favor
and return it for me. Okay.

737
00:49:17,037 --> 00:49:18,371
And, Peter?

738
00:49:18,873 --> 00:49:20,123
Take it slow.

739
00:49:20,207 --> 00:49:21,166
(CH UCKLES)

740
00:49:21,250 --> 00:49:23,126
Where did they
dig you up?

741
00:49:24,420 --> 00:49:26,713
You're gonna find
this hard to believe...

742
00:49:27,965 --> 00:49:29,716
but, uh, you sent me.

743
00:49:29,884 --> 00:49:32,051
You and Charles.

744
00:49:32,219 --> 00:49:33,803
From the future.

745
00:49:48,194 --> 00:49:49,194
(SIGHS)

746
00:49:56,243 --> 00:49:58,411
How did you lose them?

747
00:49:58,579 --> 00:50:00,830
The treatment for my
spine affects my DNA.

748
00:50:03,667 --> 00:50:06,169
You sacrificed your powers
so you could walk?

749
00:50:07,004 --> 00:50:10,173
I sacrificed my powers
so that I could sleep.

750
00:50:12,635 --> 00:50:13,760
What do you know about it?

751
00:50:13,928 --> 00:50:15,178
I've lost my fair share.

752
00:50:15,262 --> 00:50:16,262
Ha.

753
00:50:16,680 --> 00:50:18,431
Dry your eyes, Erik.

754
00:50:18,599 --> 00:50:20,266
It doesn't justify
what you've done.

755
00:50:20,434 --> 00:50:22,101
You have no idea
what I've done.

756
00:50:22,269 --> 00:50:23,937
I know that you took the
things that mean the most to me.

757
00:50:24,271 --> 00:50:26,523
Well, maybe you should have
fought harder for them.

758
00:50:26,607 --> 00:50:27,899
If you want a fight,
Erik...

759
00:50:27,983 --> 00:50:29,526
LOGAN: Sit down.
... I will give you a fight!

760
00:50:29,610 --> 00:50:30,735
Let him come.

761
00:50:30,819 --> 00:50:32,570
You abandoned me!

762
00:50:32,655 --> 00:50:33,863
You took her away...

763
00:50:33,948 --> 00:50:35,031
and you abandoned me!

764
00:50:35,199 --> 00:50:36,616
Angel.

765
00:50:36,951 --> 00:50:38,284
Azazel.

766
00:50:38,953 --> 00:50:40,787
Emma.

767
00:50:40,955 --> 00:50:42,330
Banshee.

768
00:50:43,290 --> 00:50:44,958
Mutant brothers
and sisters...

769
00:50:45,125 --> 00:50:46,584
all dead!

770
00:50:48,837 --> 00:50:50,547
(GRU NTS)
Countless others...

771
00:50:50,631 --> 00:50:51,673
experimented on.

772
00:50:51,757 --> 00:50:52,799
Butchered!

773
00:50:52,883 --> 00:50:53,883
Erik!

774
00:50:53,968 --> 00:50:55,093
Where were you, Charles?

775
00:50:55,469 --> 00:50:57,762
We were supposed
to protect them!

776
00:50:58,305 --> 00:51:00,640
Where were you when your
own people needed you?

777
00:51:00,808 --> 00:51:02,892
Hiding! You and Hank!

778
00:51:03,310 --> 00:51:05,061
Pretending to be
something you're not!

779
00:51:05,646 --> 00:51:07,021
Erik!

780
00:51:08,857 --> 00:51:11,401
You abandoned us all.

781
00:51:18,993 --> 00:51:19,993
(SIGH ING)

782
00:51:21,996 --> 00:51:23,997
(PANTING)

783
00:51:31,547 --> 00:51:33,756
So, you were
always an asshole.

784
00:51:35,217 --> 00:51:36,259
(SCOFFS)

785
00:51:36,343 --> 00:51:38,886
I take it we're best
buddies in the future.

786
00:51:38,971 --> 00:51:39,971
(CH UCKLES)

787
00:51:40,514 --> 00:51:41,889
I spent a lot of years

788
00:51:41,974 --> 00:51:43,683
trying to bring
you down, bub.

789
00:51:44,268 --> 00:51:46,019
How does that
work out for you?

790
00:51:46,186 --> 00:51:47,895
You're like me.

791
00:51:49,064 --> 00:51:50,815
You're a survivor.

792
00:51:54,903 --> 00:51:56,195
Do you wanna pick
all that shit up?

793
00:51:58,324 --> 00:52:00,617
(FRENCH DISCO MUSIC PLAYING)

794
00:52:01,619 --> 00:52:03,286
(ALL LAUGH ING)

795
00:52:09,251 --> 00:52:10,418
(SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

796
00:52:12,421 --> 00:52:13,421
(LAUGHS)

797
00:52:13,756 --> 00:52:14,964
(SPEAKING VIETNAMESE)

798
00:52:15,049 --> 00:52:19,594
General, maybe you should slow down,
we have a big day tomorrow.

799
00:52:20,554 --> 00:52:26,267
We're celebrating, captain. It's not every day you win
a war, let alone against the American devils.

800
00:52:28,479 --> 00:52:30,104
I'm getting another bottle.

801
00:52:46,080 --> 00:52:47,080
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

802
00:52:47,164 --> 00:52:48,206
Excuse me.

803
00:52:48,290 --> 00:52:49,332
(SPEAKING VIETNAMESE)

804
00:52:49,416 --> 00:52:51,376
I'm pretty sure it was my fault.

805
00:52:51,752 --> 00:52:53,169
You speak Vietnamese.

806
00:52:53,420 --> 00:52:54,504
I'm an interpreter.

807
00:52:56,507 --> 00:52:59,008
I speak many tongues.

808
00:52:59,760 --> 00:53:01,928
Let me buy you another drink...

809
00:53:02,262 --> 00:53:04,347
unless you're here with someone.

810
00:53:05,057 --> 00:53:07,392
I'm alone.

811
00:53:07,601 --> 00:53:08,559
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

812
00:53:08,644 --> 00:53:10,937
A bottle of Johnnie Walker please.

813
00:53:24,618 --> 00:53:25,618
(SPEAKING VIETNAMESE)

814
00:53:25,703 --> 00:53:28,371
You're going to the Summit tomorrow?

815
00:53:33,460 --> 00:53:38,464
A pretty girl interested in politics...

816
00:53:38,549 --> 00:53:41,134
Looks can be deceiving.

817
00:53:41,552 --> 00:53:43,010
Lady.

818
00:53:43,804 --> 00:53:47,014
Show me more, baby?

819
00:53:48,809 --> 00:53:51,394
Clothes off?

820
00:54:03,866 --> 00:54:07,869
What's the matter, baby? You don't
think I look pretty like this?

821
00:54:08,704 --> 00:54:09,704
(GRU NTS)

822
00:54:09,788 --> 00:54:10,788
(GLASS SHATTERS)

823
00:54:10,914 --> 00:54:12,665
(CHOKING)

824
00:54:14,209 --> 00:54:15,209
(GASPING)

825
00:54:33,937 --> 00:54:35,688
(SQU EAKING)
(GASPING)

826
00:54:37,775 --> 00:54:39,692
(SNORING)

827
00:54:54,416 --> 00:54:57,210
Fancy a game?
It's been a while.

828
00:54:57,377 --> 00:54:59,045
I'm not in the mood
for games, thank you.

829
00:55:05,928 --> 00:55:08,846
ERIK: I haven't had
a real sip in ten years.

830
00:55:12,434 --> 00:55:13,559
(SIGHS)

831
00:55:16,772 --> 00:55:17,772
(SWALLOWS)

832
00:55:21,652 --> 00:55:22,985
I didn't kill
the President.

833
00:55:23,779 --> 00:55:26,072
The bullet curved, Erik.

834
00:55:26,240 --> 00:55:27,740
Because I was
trying to save him.

835
00:55:29,284 --> 00:55:30,827
They took me out
before I could.

836
00:55:30,994 --> 00:55:32,036
Why would you
try and save him?

837
00:55:32,120 --> 00:55:34,747
Because he was one of us.

838
00:55:38,502 --> 00:55:39,669
(SCOFFS)

839
00:55:45,926 --> 00:55:48,344
You must think me
so foolish.

840
00:55:49,930 --> 00:55:51,931
We've always said they
would come after us.

841
00:55:52,099 --> 00:55:55,434
I never imagined they'd
use Raven's DNA to do it.

842
00:55:56,311 --> 00:55:57,603
When did you last see her?

843
00:55:57,980 --> 00:55:59,105
(CLICKS TONGU E)

844
00:56:01,275 --> 00:56:03,150
The day I left for Dallas.

845
00:56:04,152 --> 00:56:05,444
And how was she?

846
00:56:07,447 --> 00:56:08,447
Strong.

847
00:56:09,324 --> 00:56:10,324
Driven.

848
00:56:11,493 --> 00:56:12,535
Loyal.

849
00:56:12,619 --> 00:56:15,371
How... How was she?

850
00:56:17,124 --> 00:56:18,291
She was...

851
00:56:20,043 --> 00:56:21,794
We were...

852
00:56:25,299 --> 00:56:27,633
I could see why she
meant so much to you.

853
00:56:30,220 --> 00:56:31,888
You should be proud
of her, Charles.

854
00:56:33,473 --> 00:56:35,349
She's out there
fighting for our cause.

855
00:56:35,517 --> 00:56:36,893
Your cause.

856
00:56:37,686 --> 00:56:40,479
The girl I raised was
not capable of killing.

857
00:56:40,647 --> 00:56:42,148
You didn't raise her,
you grew up with her.

858
00:56:42,316 --> 00:56:44,358
She couldn't stay a little girl
forever, that's why she left.

859
00:56:44,526 --> 00:56:47,403
She left because you
got inside her head.

860
00:56:49,406 --> 00:56:51,324
That's not my power.

861
00:56:53,327 --> 00:56:54,660
She made a choice.

862
00:56:54,828 --> 00:56:57,663
But now we know where
that choice leads, don't we?

863
00:56:57,998 --> 00:56:59,248
She's going to
murder Trask,

864
00:56:59,333 --> 00:57:00,499
they're going
to capture her...

865
00:57:01,168 --> 00:57:03,419
and then they're
going to wipe us out.

866
00:57:03,587 --> 00:57:05,504
Not if we get
to her first.

867
00:57:06,715 --> 00:57:08,925
Not if we change
history tomorrow.

868
00:57:14,431 --> 00:57:16,098
I'm sorry, Charles...

869
00:57:20,520 --> 00:57:21,520
for what happened.

870
00:57:22,356 --> 00:57:23,689
I truly am.

871
00:57:27,778 --> 00:57:29,111
It's been a while since
I've played. (CLEARS TH ROAT)

872
00:57:32,199 --> 00:57:33,574
I'll go easy on you.

873
00:57:35,452 --> 00:57:37,370
Might finally
be a fair fight.

874
00:57:38,705 --> 00:57:40,081
You have the first move.

875
00:57:54,221 --> 00:57:56,931
The diplomats from
all around the world

876
00:57:57,015 --> 00:57:59,058
are arriving here
today at the Hotel Royal.

877
00:57:59,226 --> 00:58:00,643
It's an historic day.

878
00:58:00,811 --> 00:58:03,062
It's the, uh,
official ending

879
00:58:03,146 --> 00:58:05,898
of the United States' military
involvement in Vietnam.

880
00:58:06,108 --> 00:58:08,234
There we have the South
Vietnamese Foreign Minister...

881
00:58:08,402 --> 00:58:10,069
with other South
Vietnamese dignitaries.

882
00:58:10,988 --> 00:58:13,239
The Summit doesn't begin
for another hour.

883
00:58:13,407 --> 00:58:14,949
The hotel has arranged
a private room

884
00:58:15,033 --> 00:58:16,575
upstairs for
your special guests.

885
00:58:16,743 --> 00:58:18,703
TRASK: That will be
plenty of time.

886
00:58:18,787 --> 00:58:20,454
(IN DISTINCT CONVERSATIONS)

887
00:58:22,833 --> 00:58:26,794
Good afternoon, everyone.
Hello, thank you for coming.

888
00:58:26,962 --> 00:58:29,588
Congratulations on
winning this war.

889
00:58:30,090 --> 00:58:32,216
Now, I know you all
have hands to shake

890
00:58:32,300 --> 00:58:34,427
and photos to
take downstairs...

891
00:58:34,594 --> 00:58:36,637
so I will get
right to the point.

892
00:58:37,431 --> 00:58:39,682
There is a new
enemy out there.

893
00:58:39,850 --> 00:58:42,351
An enemy that will render
your arsenals useless...

894
00:58:42,519 --> 00:58:43,811
your armies powerless...

895
00:58:43,979 --> 00:58:45,855
and your nations
defenseless.

896
00:58:51,611 --> 00:58:55,489
TRASK: You will need a new weapon
for this war. I call them Sentinels.

897
00:58:57,325 --> 00:58:59,243
Named after
the ancient guardians

898
00:58:59,327 --> 00:59:01,203
that stood at
the gates of the citadel.

899
00:59:01,788 --> 00:59:03,122
(GRU NTS)

900
00:59:03,457 --> 00:59:06,292
They have the aeronautic
capabilities of a Harrier jet.

901
00:59:07,294 --> 00:59:09,628
Armed with guns
that can fire off...

902
00:59:09,796 --> 00:59:13,799
more than 2,000 rounds per minute
of thermoceramic ammunition.

903
00:59:13,967 --> 00:59:16,469
But size, power,
speed...

904
00:59:16,636 --> 00:59:18,554
you could find that
at Lockheed or Boeing.

905
00:59:18,722 --> 00:59:21,223
No, what makes the
Sentinels so special...

906
00:59:21,391 --> 00:59:24,852
is the ability to target
the mutant X-gene.

907
00:59:25,020 --> 00:59:26,520
A genetic
guidance system

908
00:59:26,646 --> 00:59:29,190
that can lock onto a mark a half a
mile away. (SPEAKING IN DISTINCTLY)

909
00:59:29,357 --> 00:59:32,359
It won't trigger unless it
has identified the target.

910
00:59:32,527 --> 00:59:34,361
With this weapon,
there will be

911
00:59:34,446 --> 00:59:36,072
no human
collateral damage.

912
00:59:36,239 --> 00:59:39,075
If I turn it on, the system
couldn't even activate in here.

913
00:59:39,701 --> 00:59:40,868
(BEEPING)

914
00:59:46,833 --> 00:59:50,669
Unless there's a mutant.

915
00:59:57,177 --> 00:59:58,177
(SPEAKING VIETNAMESE)

916
00:59:59,221 --> 01:00:01,931
There has to be
some kind of mistake.

917
01:00:03,558 --> 01:00:06,227
My machines
don't make mistakes.

918
01:00:06,561 --> 01:00:07,770
(SPEAKING VIETNAMESE)

919
01:00:08,688 --> 01:00:10,064
What are you?
(MAN SPEAKS VIETNAMESE)

920
01:00:11,024 --> 01:00:12,775
I assure you...

921
01:00:14,861 --> 01:00:15,861
TRASK: No, don't shoot it.

922
01:00:16,530 --> 01:00:17,780
I assure you,

923
01:00:17,864 --> 01:00:19,365
I don't know what
you're talking about.

924
01:00:19,449 --> 01:00:20,950
(SPEAKING VIETNAMESE)

925
01:00:27,999 --> 01:00:29,583
(GRU NTING)

926
01:00:53,817 --> 01:00:54,859
ERIK: Raven!

927
01:00:57,904 --> 01:00:59,280
(GRU NTS)

928
01:01:00,282 --> 01:01:02,158
Raven? Raven!

929
01:01:03,910 --> 01:01:05,536
(SH U DDERING)

930
01:01:06,246 --> 01:01:07,580
Raven?

931
01:01:07,664 --> 01:01:08,998
(BEEPING)

932
01:01:09,749 --> 01:01:10,916
Charles?

933
01:01:11,084 --> 01:01:13,335
We've come for you,
Erik and I.

934
01:01:13,503 --> 01:01:14,503
Together.

935
01:01:15,505 --> 01:01:17,673
RAVEN: I never thought
I'd see you again.

936
01:01:17,841 --> 01:01:20,092
CHARLES: I made you
a promise a long time ago

937
01:01:20,177 --> 01:01:21,302
that I would protect you.

938
01:01:22,053 --> 01:01:23,596
(GRU NTING)

939
01:01:29,060 --> 01:01:30,102
MAN: Wolverine!

940
01:01:30,353 --> 01:01:31,937
(GASPING)

941
01:01:34,316 --> 01:01:35,524
CHARLES: I'm going
to keep you safe.

942
01:01:35,692 --> 01:01:37,318
I'm going to keep you
out of their hands.

943
01:01:41,281 --> 01:01:42,615
Erik?

944
01:01:43,783 --> 01:01:45,951
Erik?
What are you doing?

945
01:01:47,621 --> 01:01:49,163
Securing our future.

946
01:01:49,873 --> 01:01:51,290
Forgive me,
Mystique.

947
01:01:51,666 --> 01:01:54,126
As long as you're out
there, we'll never be safe.

948
01:01:55,295 --> 01:01:56,420
Erik...

949
01:01:56,504 --> 01:01:58,505
Use your power,
Charles. Stop him.

950
01:01:58,673 --> 01:01:59,798
He can't.

951
01:02:22,405 --> 01:02:23,989
(CROWD GASPING)

952
01:02:27,535 --> 01:02:28,869
(GROAN ING)

953
01:02:30,664 --> 01:02:32,164
KITTY: He's slipping back.

954
01:02:32,332 --> 01:02:33,540
I'm losing him.

955
01:02:37,420 --> 01:02:38,754
(PANTING)

956
01:02:41,049 --> 01:02:42,466
(GRU NTING)

957
01:02:56,022 --> 01:02:57,606
(CROWD EXCLAIMING)

958
01:03:05,865 --> 01:03:07,116
(ALL GASPING)

959
01:03:15,208 --> 01:03:16,250
LOGAN: Stryker!

960
01:03:16,710 --> 01:03:18,836
STRYKER: Someone will finish
what we've started, Wolverine!

961
01:03:18,920 --> 01:03:19,962
One day!

962
01:03:20,046 --> 01:03:21,505
(GRU NTING)
(SCREAMS)

963
01:03:25,427 --> 01:03:26,427
Restrain him.

964
01:03:27,512 --> 01:03:28,887
(CROWD CLAMORING)

965
01:03:30,765 --> 01:03:32,057
(GROAN ING)

966
01:03:39,065 --> 01:03:40,441
(SCREAMING)

967
01:03:41,568 --> 01:03:42,568
Erik!

968
01:03:52,746 --> 01:03:53,829
Where am I?

969
01:03:53,913 --> 01:03:54,955
Huh?

970
01:03:56,791 --> 01:03:58,083
How the hell
did I get here?

971
01:03:58,251 --> 01:03:59,835
What? You came to us.

972
01:04:00,837 --> 01:04:02,087
Who are you?
Charles.

973
01:04:02,589 --> 01:04:03,756
Charles Xavier!

974
01:04:03,840 --> 01:04:04,840
I don't know you.

975
01:04:04,924 --> 01:04:06,967
Huh?
What the hell is that?

976
01:04:07,093 --> 01:04:10,471
Whoa. Whoa. Look, I can
deal with this. Just go.

977
01:04:10,764 --> 01:04:12,139
Stop Erik!

978
01:04:12,599 --> 01:04:13,724
Erik, please...

979
01:04:13,808 --> 01:04:14,933
I'm sorry.

980
01:04:15,101 --> 01:04:16,268
Erik...

981
01:04:16,686 --> 01:04:18,062
(CROWD SCREAMING)

982
01:04:19,856 --> 01:04:20,856
(GROAN ING)

983
01:04:28,114 --> 01:04:29,948
(CROWD SCREAMING)

984
01:04:30,867 --> 01:04:31,950
(GASPS)

985
01:04:35,038 --> 01:04:37,331
You're Logan, that's Hank
McCoy, I'm Charles Xavier.

986
01:04:37,499 --> 01:04:39,958
You spent the last
couple of days with us.

987
01:04:43,338 --> 01:04:44,963
You're on acid.

988
01:04:45,799 --> 01:04:49,843
Somebody gave you
really bad acid, yeah?

989
01:04:52,180 --> 01:04:53,222
(RATTLING)

990
01:05:02,565 --> 01:05:03,982
(ALL SCREAMING)

991
01:05:33,179 --> 01:05:34,263
(GRU NTS)

992
01:05:34,514 --> 01:05:35,597
Just hold on tight,

993
01:05:35,682 --> 01:05:36,890
we'll get through
this together.

994
01:05:36,975 --> 01:05:38,308
(KITTY GROANS)

995
01:05:38,393 --> 01:05:39,685
Oh, my God, Kitty.

996
01:05:41,855 --> 01:05:42,855
She's wounded
pretty bad.

997
01:05:45,191 --> 01:05:46,233
(GROAN ING)

998
01:05:56,619 --> 01:05:57,744
(CLAMORING)

999
01:06:30,904 --> 01:06:32,154
(ROARING)

1000
01:06:38,077 --> 01:06:39,912
(KITTY WH IMPERING)

1001
01:06:48,171 --> 01:06:49,254
I got him.

1002
01:06:50,590 --> 01:06:51,590
(GASPS)

1003
01:06:54,010 --> 01:06:55,010
Professor?

1004
01:06:55,762 --> 01:06:56,845
What happened to you?

1005
01:06:58,431 --> 01:06:59,765
I just saw someone
who's gonna

1006
01:06:59,849 --> 01:07:01,433
bring me a lot
of pain someday.

1007
01:07:02,644 --> 01:07:04,061
(POLICE SIRENS WAILING)

1008
01:07:04,270 --> 01:07:05,270
Where's Raven?

1009
01:07:05,939 --> 01:07:07,189
Gone.
What?

1010
01:07:07,357 --> 01:07:09,399
We have to get
out of here.

1011
01:07:09,734 --> 01:07:11,777
We want to know if there's
any sort of connection with...

1012
01:07:11,986 --> 01:07:13,320
(ALL CLAMORING)

1013
01:07:18,368 --> 01:07:20,035
Yesterday,
the Paris Peace Summit...

1014
01:07:20,203 --> 01:07:22,913
was rocked by the appearance
of unidentified assailants...

1015
01:07:23,039 --> 01:07:25,332
the likes of which
the world has never seen.

1016
01:07:25,500 --> 01:07:28,210
Mass hysteria has gripped
the nation as people ask...

1017
01:07:28,378 --> 01:07:30,629
"Where did they come from?
Will they be back?"

1018
01:07:30,797 --> 01:07:33,715
And most importantly,
"Are they friend or foe?"

1019
01:07:33,883 --> 01:07:36,885
That was London
correspondent Toby Elliot...

1020
01:07:37,011 --> 01:07:38,554
reporting from the
Paris Peace Summit yesterday.

1021
01:07:40,056 --> 01:07:42,683
What the hell are we dealing
with here? Off the record.

1022
01:07:43,476 --> 01:07:46,853
Two days ago, this
man, Erik Lehnsherr...

1023
01:07:47,021 --> 01:07:49,523
escaped from a maximum security
prison inside the Pentagon.

1024
01:07:49,691 --> 01:07:51,567
We believe
that this woman

1025
01:07:51,651 --> 01:07:53,402
is a former associate
of Lehnsherr's.

1026
01:07:53,570 --> 01:07:55,070
They were together
in Cuba,

1027
01:07:55,154 --> 01:07:57,573
the day of
the crisis in '62.

1028
01:07:57,740 --> 01:08:01,410
He was also implicated
in Kennedy's assassination.

1029
01:08:02,537 --> 01:08:03,912
What about that thing?

1030
01:08:04,080 --> 01:08:05,581
MAN: We don't know what
that thing is, sir.

1031
01:08:05,748 --> 01:08:08,041
Actually, we really don't
know what any of them are.

1032
01:08:08,209 --> 01:08:10,752
Yes. Yes, we do.

1033
01:08:11,588 --> 01:08:13,005
They're mutants.

1034
01:08:14,382 --> 01:08:18,343
He has the power
to control metal.

1035
01:08:18,511 --> 01:08:19,761
Last I checked,
that's what

1036
01:08:19,846 --> 01:08:21,346
most of your weapons
were made of.

1037
01:08:21,556 --> 01:08:25,392
And she can transform
into anyone.

1038
01:08:25,560 --> 01:08:28,353
A general,
a secret serviceman.

1039
01:08:28,521 --> 01:08:29,771
Even you,
Mr. President.

1040
01:08:30,440 --> 01:08:31,690
She could walk
into this office...

1041
01:08:31,858 --> 01:08:35,527
and order a nuclear strike
if she was in the mood.

1042
01:08:35,695 --> 01:08:37,279
And that's only
two of them.

1043
01:08:37,447 --> 01:08:40,449
Do we have any
countermeasures? Any defense?

1044
01:08:40,617 --> 01:08:42,868
I was waiting for you
to ask me that question.

1045
01:08:43,202 --> 01:08:46,955
That's an experimental program,
sir. Strictly off the books.

1046
01:08:53,212 --> 01:08:54,546
(DOG BARKS)

1047
01:08:55,757 --> 01:08:58,425
You're telling me these
mutants are out in the world...

1048
01:08:58,593 --> 01:09:01,053
and our best defense
are these giant metal robots?

1049
01:09:01,220 --> 01:09:03,263
Many of the mutants
look like us.

1050
01:09:03,723 --> 01:09:05,891
My Sentinels can
tell the difference.

1051
01:09:06,142 --> 01:09:08,435
I have eight prototypes
ready to go.

1052
01:09:08,603 --> 01:09:10,520
They're built out of
a space-age polymer,

1053
01:09:10,605 --> 01:09:12,272
not an ounce
of metal on them.

1054
01:09:18,905 --> 01:09:20,238
I want to make
a demonstration.

1055
01:09:20,406 --> 01:09:22,658
I want the world to know
that we can protect them.

1056
01:09:23,159 --> 01:09:24,785
What do you need to get
these things operational?

1057
01:09:24,952 --> 01:09:26,495
I already gave that
number to Congress.

1058
01:09:26,663 --> 01:09:29,414
Unfortunately, they
elected to shut me down.

1059
01:09:29,582 --> 01:09:32,167
It's going to cost a
bit more to turn them on.

1060
01:09:32,335 --> 01:09:33,377
N IXON: Whatever you need.

1061
01:09:33,461 --> 01:09:35,337
TRASK: Oh,
and one more thing.

1062
01:09:35,505 --> 01:09:38,924
If we do manage to capture
them, I would like her.

1063
01:09:39,092 --> 01:09:41,009
For research purposes,
of course.

1064
01:09:43,763 --> 01:09:45,097
(N EWSREADER SPEAKING FRENCH)

1065
01:09:45,765 --> 01:09:46,765
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

1066
01:09:46,849 --> 01:09:48,266
Terrible thing.

1067
01:09:49,435 --> 01:09:50,811
What is?

1068
01:09:51,270 --> 01:09:52,771
Being born like that.

1069
01:09:52,855 --> 01:09:53,980
Is it?

1070
01:09:54,315 --> 01:09:56,608
Can you imagine...

1071
01:09:56,859 --> 01:09:59,528
Looking in the mirror and seeing that
staring back at you?

1072
01:10:00,613 --> 01:10:03,365
Yes, I can.

1073
01:10:05,618 --> 01:10:08,245
Where do you think she comes from?

1074
01:10:08,496 --> 01:10:11,289
You think she has a family?

1075
01:10:12,959 --> 01:10:14,501
Yes.

1076
01:10:14,669 --> 01:10:16,503
She does.

1077
01:10:19,507 --> 01:10:22,092
(N EWSREADER SPEAKING
FRENCH ON TV)

1078
01:10:54,542 --> 01:10:55,917
(BEGGING IN FRENCH)

1079
01:11:04,218 --> 01:11:06,261
If I see so much
as a screw move,

1080
01:11:06,345 --> 01:11:08,346
I will jam this
into your throat.

1081
01:11:09,098 --> 01:11:10,682
How did you find me?

1082
01:11:10,850 --> 01:11:12,350
You taught me well.

1083
01:11:12,518 --> 01:11:14,853
It's been a long time
since we were this close.

1084
01:11:16,355 --> 01:11:17,731
I missed you.

1085
01:11:17,899 --> 01:11:19,566
You tried to kill me.

1086
01:11:19,734 --> 01:11:21,860
So the rest of us
could live.

1087
01:11:23,362 --> 01:11:24,613
What do you mean?

1088
01:11:25,198 --> 01:11:27,199
We received a message
from the future.

1089
01:11:27,366 --> 01:11:29,284
Don't lie to me.

1090
01:11:29,911 --> 01:11:31,912
I never have,
and I never will.

1091
01:11:33,539 --> 01:11:35,957
Humans use your blood,
your genes,

1092
01:11:36,042 --> 01:11:38,418
to create a weapon
that wipes us all out.

1093
01:11:38,586 --> 01:11:40,003
I was only doing
what I thought

1094
01:11:40,087 --> 01:11:42,047
necessary to secure
our future.

1095
01:11:42,215 --> 01:11:43,507
So what's to stop me
from killing you

1096
01:11:43,591 --> 01:11:45,383
right now and
securing my future?

1097
01:11:46,427 --> 01:11:47,552
Nothing.

1098
01:11:48,805 --> 01:11:50,722
It doesn't matter
anymore.

1099
01:11:50,890 --> 01:11:53,725
They have your DNA. Your
blood was on the street.

1100
01:11:54,393 --> 01:11:55,727
Whose fault was that?

1101
01:11:57,396 --> 01:11:58,814
Mine.

1102
01:11:59,732 --> 01:12:03,068
I've seen their plans.
They're creating a weapon.

1103
01:12:03,236 --> 01:12:06,154
And now they have what they
need to take it further.

1104
01:12:08,449 --> 01:12:11,785
We have to strike now, while
we still hold the upper hand.

1105
01:12:14,622 --> 01:12:16,665
I've seen too many
friends die, Erik.

1106
01:12:18,751 --> 01:12:21,002
I don't want a war.

1107
01:12:21,087 --> 01:12:22,921
I only want the man
who murdered them.

1108
01:12:23,089 --> 01:12:24,589
This is war.

1109
01:12:26,425 --> 01:12:28,260
What happened to you?

1110
01:12:29,095 --> 01:12:31,346
Did you lose your way
while I was gone?

1111
01:12:33,349 --> 01:12:35,433
Are you still Charles' Raven?

1112
01:12:37,770 --> 01:12:40,188
Or are you Mystique?

1113
01:12:43,609 --> 01:12:45,151
Trask is the enemy.

1114
01:12:47,321 --> 01:12:49,364
Killing one man isn't enough.

1115
01:12:49,782 --> 01:12:51,116
It never was for you.

1116
01:12:52,493 --> 01:12:53,702
Goodbye, Erik.

1117
01:13:17,143 --> 01:13:18,810
(GRU NTING)

1118
01:13:18,936 --> 01:13:20,103
LOGAN: What happened?

1119
01:13:20,187 --> 01:13:21,813
Come on.
Can he walk?

1120
01:13:21,981 --> 01:13:23,148
He needs his treatment.

1121
01:13:23,649 --> 01:13:24,774
Hank, I can hear them.

1122
01:13:24,859 --> 01:13:25,984
I know. It's okay.

1123
01:13:26,152 --> 01:13:28,194
Can you make it stop?
I'll get them.

1124
01:13:28,654 --> 01:13:30,071
(GROANS)

1125
01:13:30,197 --> 01:13:31,323
LOGAN: Hey, hey.

1126
01:13:31,449 --> 01:13:33,158
Pull yourself together.

1127
01:13:33,326 --> 01:13:34,826
It's not over yet.
(PANTING)

1128
01:13:37,997 --> 01:13:39,372
You don't believe that.

1129
01:13:41,292 --> 01:13:42,667
How do you know?

1130
01:13:42,835 --> 01:13:44,502
CHARLES: As these go...

1131
01:13:46,213 --> 01:13:49,507
this comes back.

1132
01:13:50,176 --> 01:13:52,510
They all come back.

1133
01:13:57,683 --> 01:13:59,100
Look.

1134
01:13:59,852 --> 01:14:01,519
I'm still here...

1135
01:14:02,563 --> 01:14:04,064
and she's still out there.

1136
01:14:06,233 --> 01:14:08,360
We need your help, Charles.

1137
01:14:08,945 --> 01:14:10,528
Not like this.
I need you.

1138
01:14:10,988 --> 01:14:14,240
We can't find Raven.
Not without your powers.

1139
01:14:14,700 --> 01:14:16,117
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACH ING)

1140
01:14:17,870 --> 01:14:20,205
HAN K: I added a little extra
because you missed a dose.

1141
01:14:21,874 --> 01:14:23,249
(BREATH ING H EAVILY)

1142
01:14:25,878 --> 01:14:27,045
Charles.

1143
01:14:51,070 --> 01:14:52,445
(IN HALES SHARPLY)

1144
01:14:58,411 --> 01:15:00,537
Hank, do me a favor.

1145
01:15:01,247 --> 01:15:03,540
Would you help me
to my study, please?

1146
01:15:08,546 --> 01:15:10,296
Come on, I got you.
(CHARLES GRU NTS)

1147
01:15:20,433 --> 01:15:22,726
Are you sure
about this?

1148
01:15:24,103 --> 01:15:26,229
Absolutely not.

1149
01:15:32,778 --> 01:15:34,946
TRASK: This creature
is extraordinary.

1150
01:15:36,157 --> 01:15:37,782
Her genes could hold the key

1151
01:15:37,867 --> 01:15:39,909
to mutation itself.

1152
01:15:39,994 --> 01:15:41,077
I need more.

1153
01:15:41,162 --> 01:15:43,997
That's all they were able to
scrape off the pavement in Paris.

1154
01:15:44,165 --> 01:15:45,331
More than blood.

1155
01:15:45,833 --> 01:15:47,625
I need brain tissue...

1156
01:15:47,793 --> 01:15:50,420
spinal fluid, bone marrow.

1157
01:15:51,547 --> 01:15:52,714
Imagine...

1158
01:15:52,798 --> 01:15:54,340
Sentinels that
could transform,

1159
01:15:54,425 --> 01:15:55,675
adapt to any target.

1160
01:15:56,469 --> 01:15:58,595
If I could just get
my hands on her.

1161
01:15:58,763 --> 01:16:00,597
This girl could leap

1162
01:16:00,681 --> 01:16:02,432
the program forward years...

1163
01:16:02,600 --> 01:16:04,476
decades into the future.

1164
01:16:05,811 --> 01:16:07,103
How old is your
son now, Major?

1165
01:16:08,439 --> 01:16:09,522
Jason?

1166
01:16:09,690 --> 01:16:11,691
He's coming up on ten now,
if you can believe it.

1167
01:16:11,776 --> 01:16:13,276
Eight years
from fighting age.

1168
01:16:13,527 --> 01:16:15,361
And how many of
our sons and brothers

1169
01:16:15,446 --> 01:16:17,197
did we just ship
home in body bags?

1170
01:16:17,364 --> 01:16:19,324
Maybe fifty,
fifty-five thousand?

1171
01:16:19,492 --> 01:16:20,950
And how many more
on the other side?

1172
01:16:22,495 --> 01:16:24,329
Never before...

1173
01:16:24,497 --> 01:16:27,499
in all of human history...

1174
01:16:27,666 --> 01:16:32,337
has there been a cause which
could unite us as a species.

1175
01:16:33,339 --> 01:16:35,673
Until now.

1176
01:16:36,967 --> 01:16:38,968
You really hate,
mutants, don't you?

1177
01:16:39,136 --> 01:16:42,472
On the contrary,
I rather admire them.

1178
01:16:42,640 --> 01:16:43,723
The things they can do.

1179
01:16:45,392 --> 01:16:48,353
I see mutants
as our salvation.

1180
01:16:48,521 --> 01:16:49,687
A common enemy.

1181
01:16:50,523 --> 01:16:53,650
A common struggle
against the ultimate enemy.

1182
01:16:54,318 --> 01:16:56,194
Extinction.

1183
01:16:56,654 --> 01:16:57,654
I believe
our new friends...

1184
01:16:57,822 --> 01:17:00,198
are going to help us
usher in a new era, Bill.

1185
01:17:00,366 --> 01:17:02,700
A new era of genuine...

1186
01:17:02,868 --> 01:17:05,620
and long-lasting peace.

1187
01:17:19,593 --> 01:17:21,052
MAN OVER PA:
Attention, attention.

1188
01:17:21,137 --> 01:17:23,012
Transport departure
in two hours.

1189
01:17:23,180 --> 01:17:27,183
Repeat. Transport
departure in two hours.

1190
01:17:33,357 --> 01:17:36,151
(SIGHS) When was the last
time you were down here?

1191
01:17:36,360 --> 01:17:37,735
The last time we went
looking for students.

1192
01:17:38,028 --> 01:17:39,737
A lifetime ago.

1193
01:17:43,284 --> 01:17:44,659
(ELECTRICAL WH IRRING)

1194
01:17:45,619 --> 01:17:47,787
AUTOMATED FEMALE VOICE:
Welcome, Professor.

1195
01:18:08,559 --> 01:18:10,018
(SIGH ING)

1196
01:18:11,270 --> 01:18:13,479
HAN K: Raven's wounded.
She won't be moving fast.

1197
01:18:17,026 --> 01:18:18,526
(BLOWS)

1198
01:18:21,906 --> 01:18:24,240
These are muscles I haven't
stretched in a long time.

1199
01:18:31,415 --> 01:18:32,957
(GASPS)

1200
01:18:38,964 --> 01:18:41,132
(IN DISTINCT SHOUTING)

1201
01:18:46,805 --> 01:18:48,640
(WEEPING AN D YELLING)

1202
01:18:52,645 --> 01:18:54,354
(IN DISTINCT SHOUTING
CONTIN U ES)

1203
01:19:06,659 --> 01:19:07,742
(GROAN ING)

1204
01:19:07,826 --> 01:19:08,826
Charles!

1205
01:19:11,288 --> 01:19:12,372
Charles!

1206
01:19:13,165 --> 01:19:16,084
(SCREAMING)

1207
01:19:20,297 --> 01:19:23,091
(GROANS)
Charles? It's all right.

1208
01:19:23,509 --> 01:19:24,801
(PANTING)

1209
01:19:25,678 --> 01:19:27,470
I'll go check
the generator.

1210
01:19:35,229 --> 01:19:36,813
It's not the
machinery, is it?

1211
01:19:37,648 --> 01:19:39,065
I can't do this.
My mind...

1212
01:19:39,191 --> 01:19:40,400
Yes, you can.

1213
01:19:40,526 --> 01:19:42,318
(STAMMERING) It won't take
it. You're just a little rusty.

1214
01:19:42,403 --> 01:19:44,862
You don't understand. It's
not a question of being rusty.

1215
01:19:45,030 --> 01:19:46,781
I can flip the switches.
I can turn the knobs.

1216
01:19:46,865 --> 01:19:50,493
But my power comes from
here. It comes from...

1217
01:19:51,203 --> 01:19:52,870
And it's broken.

1218
01:19:53,998 --> 01:19:55,915
I feel like one
of my students.

1219
01:19:56,208 --> 01:19:57,500
Helpless.

1220
01:19:58,877 --> 01:20:00,086
It was a mistake
coming down here.

1221
01:20:00,254 --> 01:20:01,796
It was a mistake
freeing Erik.

1222
01:20:01,880 --> 01:20:04,257
This whole thing has
been one bloody mistake.

1223
01:20:04,341 --> 01:20:06,843
I'm sorry, Logan, but they
sent back the wrong man.

1224
01:20:07,678 --> 01:20:09,095
You're right.

1225
01:20:10,431 --> 01:20:11,931
I am.

1226
01:20:12,850 --> 01:20:14,350
Actually, it was
supposed to be you.

1227
01:20:15,394 --> 01:20:18,938
But I was the only one who
could physically make the trip.

1228
01:20:19,606 --> 01:20:20,732
And, uh...

1229
01:20:21,066 --> 01:20:22,650
And I don't know
how long I've got here.

1230
01:20:23,110 --> 01:20:25,903
But I do know that
a long time ago...

1231
01:20:26,530 --> 01:20:28,906
actually, a long
time from now...

1232
01:20:29,241 --> 01:20:32,410
I was your most
helpless student.

1233
01:20:32,870 --> 01:20:35,246
And you unlocked
my mind.

1234
01:20:35,414 --> 01:20:38,082
You showed me
what I was.

1235
01:20:38,250 --> 01:20:40,084
You showed me
what I could be.

1236
01:20:40,252 --> 01:20:42,253
I don't know how
to do that for you.

1237
01:20:42,421 --> 01:20:44,380
You're right.
I don't.

1238
01:20:46,258 --> 01:20:48,301
But I know
someone who might.

1239
01:20:48,761 --> 01:20:50,345
Hmm.

1240
01:20:50,429 --> 01:20:53,389
Look into my mind.

1241
01:20:53,599 --> 01:20:55,850
You saw what
I did to Cerebro.

1242
01:20:55,934 --> 01:20:57,185
You don't want me
inside your head.

1243
01:20:57,269 --> 01:20:58,353
There's no damage
you can do...

1244
01:20:58,437 --> 01:20:59,812
that hasn't already
been done. Trust me.

1245
01:21:00,105 --> 01:21:01,105
Come on.

1246
01:21:11,492 --> 01:21:12,492
(SCREAMING)

1247
01:21:12,576 --> 01:21:13,618
Hey.

1248
01:21:14,453 --> 01:21:15,453
(SCREAMING)

1249
01:21:15,537 --> 01:21:16,579
Hey, Logan.

1250
01:21:16,663 --> 01:21:17,663
Hi, Jean.

1251
01:21:18,123 --> 01:21:19,207
Kill me.

1252
01:21:19,291 --> 01:21:20,291
I love you.

1253
01:21:21,210 --> 01:21:22,502
(GROANS)
(SCREAMING)

1254
01:21:23,587 --> 01:21:28,049
You poor, poor man.

1255
01:21:28,133 --> 01:21:29,300
Look past me.

1256
01:21:29,468 --> 01:21:31,302
No, I don't want
your suffering.

1257
01:21:31,470 --> 01:21:33,388
I don't want your future!

1258
01:21:33,472 --> 01:21:35,598
Look past my future.

1259
01:21:35,849 --> 01:21:37,975
Look for your future.

1260
01:21:41,480 --> 01:21:42,814
That's it.

1261
01:21:43,190 --> 01:21:44,440
That's it.

1262
01:21:46,151 --> 01:21:47,485
That's it.

1263
01:22:02,167 --> 01:22:03,626
(SIGHS)

1264
01:22:16,390 --> 01:22:17,723
(IN DISTINCT TALKING)

1265
01:22:35,409 --> 01:22:37,368
Charles.

1266
01:22:39,204 --> 01:22:40,580
Charles.

1267
01:22:42,416 --> 01:22:43,791
(CH UCKLES)

1268
01:22:44,835 --> 01:22:47,211
So this is what
becomes of us.

1269
01:22:48,505 --> 01:22:50,339
Erik was right.

1270
01:22:51,008 --> 01:22:53,217
Humanity
does this to us.

1271
01:22:53,385 --> 01:22:56,012
Not if we show
them a better path.

1272
01:22:56,930 --> 01:22:58,598
You still believe?

1273
01:22:58,765 --> 01:23:01,225
Just because someone
stumbles, loses their way...

1274
01:23:01,393 --> 01:23:04,228
it doesn't mean
they're lost forever.

1275
01:23:04,855 --> 01:23:08,608
Sometimes we all need
a little help.

1276
01:23:09,568 --> 01:23:11,235
Oh, I'm not
the man I was.

1277
01:23:13,405 --> 01:23:15,448
I open my mind...

1278
01:23:16,033 --> 01:23:18,242
and it almost
overwhelms me.

1279
01:23:18,577 --> 01:23:22,079
You're afraid,
and Cerebro knows it.

1280
01:23:23,248 --> 01:23:25,791
All those voices...

1281
01:23:27,544 --> 01:23:32,215
so much pain.

1282
01:23:32,591 --> 01:23:35,927
It's not their pain
you're afraid of.

1283
01:23:36,094 --> 01:23:38,095
It's yours, Charles.

1284
01:23:39,389 --> 01:23:41,891
And as frightening
as it may be...

1285
01:23:42,059 --> 01:23:44,894
that pain will
make you stronger.

1286
01:23:45,229 --> 01:23:48,272
If you allow
yourself to feel it...

1287
01:23:48,440 --> 01:23:50,149
embrace it...

1288
01:23:51,318 --> 01:23:53,194
it will make you more powerful

1289
01:23:53,278 --> 01:23:55,488
than you ever imagined.

1290
01:23:55,656 --> 01:23:57,406
It's the greatest

1291
01:23:57,491 --> 01:23:58,991
gift we have...

1292
01:23:59,159 --> 01:24:00,993
to bear their pain

1293
01:24:01,078 --> 01:24:02,995
without breaking.

1294
01:24:03,163 --> 01:24:04,956
And it's born...

1295
01:24:05,123 --> 01:24:07,500
from the most human power.

1296
01:24:08,502 --> 01:24:10,086
Hope.

1297
01:24:19,179 --> 01:24:21,514
Please, Charles...

1298
01:24:21,682 --> 01:24:25,643
we need you to hope again.

1299
01:24:33,944 --> 01:24:36,404
Find what you were
looking for?

1300
01:24:42,202 --> 01:24:43,494
HAN K: The power's
back on.

1301
01:24:43,662 --> 01:24:44,954
Yes.

1302
01:24:45,998 --> 01:24:47,707
Yes, it is.

1303
01:24:49,543 --> 01:24:50,543
(TRAIN WH ISTLE BLOWING)

1304
01:25:07,853 --> 01:25:08,853
(GRU NTS)

1305
01:25:13,650 --> 01:25:15,151
(METAL CLAN KING)

1306
01:25:52,731 --> 01:25:54,148
(ELECTRICAL WH IRRING)

1307
01:26:13,126 --> 01:26:14,710
(BREATH ING H EAVILY)

1308
01:26:14,961 --> 01:26:16,462
(WIN D HOWLING)

1309
01:26:26,973 --> 01:26:27,973
(MOAN ING)

1310
01:26:28,058 --> 01:26:29,475
BOBBY: She's lost
too much blood.

1311
01:26:30,102 --> 01:26:31,435
She can't keep
going like this.

1312
01:26:31,603 --> 01:26:33,771
We have no choice,
Bobby.

1313
01:26:33,939 --> 01:26:35,272
We can wake him up.
No!

1314
01:26:36,900 --> 01:26:38,150
They need more time.

1315
01:26:38,735 --> 01:26:40,778
I had...

1316
01:26:41,321 --> 01:26:43,322
a glimpse into the past.

1317
01:26:43,490 --> 01:26:44,907
If we wake Logan now...

1318
01:26:45,075 --> 01:26:48,452
we may set our fate
on an even darker course.

1319
01:26:48,662 --> 01:26:50,454
They need more time.

1320
01:26:54,543 --> 01:26:55,626
(SIGHS)

1321
01:26:56,336 --> 01:26:57,628
(KITTY GROAN ING)

1322
01:27:02,801 --> 01:27:04,802
(WOMAN AN NOU NCING
IN FRENCH OVER PA)

1323
01:27:09,808 --> 01:27:11,434
Raven, stop.

1324
01:27:12,352 --> 01:27:13,978
Stop running.

1325
01:27:14,312 --> 01:27:15,479
Charles?

1326
01:27:17,524 --> 01:27:18,607
Where are you?

1327
01:27:18,692 --> 01:27:19,900
Back at the house...

1328
01:27:19,985 --> 01:27:21,777
where you should be.

1329
01:27:21,945 --> 01:27:24,113
I need you to come home.

1330
01:27:24,823 --> 01:27:26,657
I know what
I need to do.

1331
01:27:30,328 --> 01:27:31,537
If you kill Trask...

1332
01:27:31,621 --> 01:27:33,789
you will be creating
countless more just like him.

1333
01:27:34,458 --> 01:27:35,541
Then I'll kill
them, too.

1334
01:27:35,667 --> 01:27:38,169
Those are Erik's words,
not yours.

1335
01:27:39,212 --> 01:27:40,713
Oh!

1336
01:27:41,840 --> 01:27:44,341
The girl I grew up with
wasn't capable of killing.

1337
01:27:44,468 --> 01:27:45,468
She was good...

1338
01:27:45,594 --> 01:27:48,179
fair, full of compassion.

1339
01:27:49,514 --> 01:27:51,265
I have compassion.

1340
01:27:51,349 --> 01:27:52,850
Just not for Trask.

1341
01:27:52,976 --> 01:27:54,643
He's murdered
too many of us.

1342
01:27:58,523 --> 01:28:00,399
Shut her down, Charles.
Get in her head.

1343
01:28:00,567 --> 01:28:02,026
CHARLES: She's
not letting me in.

1344
01:28:02,194 --> 01:28:05,404
I'm barely holding on.
I'm not strong enough yet.

1345
01:28:08,867 --> 01:28:11,243
(IN DISTINCT CONVERSATIONS)
(GASPS)

1346
01:28:13,538 --> 01:28:15,372
I know what
Trask has done...

1347
01:28:15,749 --> 01:28:18,083
but killing him
will not bring them back.

1348
01:28:18,710 --> 01:28:19,794
It will set you
on a path...

1349
01:28:19,878 --> 01:28:21,879
from which
there is no return.

1350
01:28:22,589 --> 01:28:24,340
An endless cycle
of killing.

1351
01:28:24,508 --> 01:28:28,219
Us and them, until
there is nothing left.

1352
01:28:29,095 --> 01:28:33,098
But we can stop it,
right now, you and I.

1353
01:28:34,017 --> 01:28:37,102
You just have to
come home.

1354
01:28:38,396 --> 01:28:40,189
I have to?

1355
01:28:40,565 --> 01:28:42,024
You haven't changed
at all, Charles.

1356
01:28:43,360 --> 01:28:44,443
Like I said...

1357
01:28:44,569 --> 01:28:46,946
I know exactly
what I have to do.

1358
01:28:52,327 --> 01:28:53,911
(IN DISTINCT CONVERSATIONS)

1359
01:29:02,254 --> 01:29:03,254
Where is she?

1360
01:29:03,421 --> 01:29:05,422
(CH UCKLES) She's in an
airport, boarding a plane.

1361
01:29:06,132 --> 01:29:07,591
LOGAN: A plane to where?

1362
01:29:10,554 --> 01:29:12,221
CHARLES: Washington, D.C.

1363
01:29:13,932 --> 01:29:17,518
Guys, there's something
I need to show you.

1364
01:29:19,938 --> 01:29:21,730
We're going
backwards in time.

1365
01:29:21,898 --> 01:29:23,899
I set the system
I designed...

1366
01:29:23,984 --> 01:29:26,360
to record any news about Paris
over all three networks...

1367
01:29:26,736 --> 01:29:27,820
and PBS.

1368
01:29:28,238 --> 01:29:29,780
All three? Wow.

1369
01:29:30,115 --> 01:29:31,782
Yeah, and PBS.

1370
01:29:32,784 --> 01:29:34,201
Look what I found.

1371
01:29:34,369 --> 01:29:35,744
Tomorrow, in front
of the White House,

1372
01:29:35,871 --> 01:29:37,246
the President will
make his announcement.

1373
01:29:37,789 --> 01:29:39,957
He will be joined by
Secretary of Defense Laird...

1374
01:29:40,125 --> 01:29:43,711
and has even sought the help of
renowned scientist Bolivar Trask...

1375
01:29:43,879 --> 01:29:47,381
his special advisor
to combat this mutant issue.

1376
01:29:47,549 --> 01:29:48,632
The White House
has asked...

1377
01:29:48,717 --> 01:29:49,884
CHARLES: Raven
doesn't realize...

1378
01:29:49,968 --> 01:29:51,844
that if she kills Trask
at an event like that...

1379
01:29:51,928 --> 01:29:54,305
with the whole
world watching...

1380
01:29:55,098 --> 01:29:57,558
Then I came a long way
for nothing.

1381
01:29:58,101 --> 01:30:00,060
HAN K: And there's more bad
news. I saw in a report...

1382
01:30:00,645 --> 01:30:02,146
they found traces
of her blood in Paris.

1383
01:30:02,480 --> 01:30:05,482
For all we know,
they already have her DNA...

1384
01:30:05,650 --> 01:30:06,775
which is all they'd need.

1385
01:30:06,860 --> 01:30:08,986
To create the Sentinels
of the future.

1386
01:30:12,574 --> 01:30:14,575
There's a theory
in quantum physics...

1387
01:30:14,659 --> 01:30:16,285
that time is immutable.

1388
01:30:16,494 --> 01:30:18,370
It's like a river. You can
throw a pebble into it...

1389
01:30:18,455 --> 01:30:21,749
and create a ripple, but the
current always corrects itself.

1390
01:30:22,667 --> 01:30:24,543
No matter what
you do, the river

1391
01:30:24,628 --> 01:30:26,420
just keeps flowing
in the same direction.

1392
01:30:26,838 --> 01:30:28,130
What are you
trying to say?

1393
01:30:28,298 --> 01:30:30,174
What I'm saying is...

1394
01:30:30,342 --> 01:30:31,926
what if the war
is inevitable?

1395
01:30:32,010 --> 01:30:34,428
What if she's meant
to kill Trask?

1396
01:30:35,972 --> 01:30:38,515
What if this is just
simply who she is?

1397
01:30:40,518 --> 01:30:44,521
Just because someone
stumbles, loses their way...

1398
01:30:44,689 --> 01:30:46,690
doesn't mean
they're lost forever.

1399
01:30:48,735 --> 01:30:50,152
(CH UCKLES)

1400
01:30:51,529 --> 01:30:54,198
No, I don't believe
that theory, Hank.

1401
01:30:55,116 --> 01:30:58,118
And I cannot believe
that is who she is.

1402
01:30:59,371 --> 01:31:00,496
Ready the plane.

1403
01:31:00,580 --> 01:31:02,998
We're going
to Washington.

1404
01:32:20,994 --> 01:32:22,494
You all right?

1405
01:32:22,620 --> 01:32:23,662
Getting there.

1406
01:32:26,791 --> 01:32:27,958
(SIGHS)

1407
01:32:28,585 --> 01:32:31,253
Whatever happens today, I need
you to promise me something.

1408
01:32:32,130 --> 01:32:35,257
You've looked into my mind
and seen a lot of bad...

1409
01:32:36,134 --> 01:32:37,801
but you've seen
the good, too.

1410
01:32:38,845 --> 01:32:40,512
The X-Men.

1411
01:32:41,765 --> 01:32:43,348
Promise me
you'll find us.

1412
01:32:45,143 --> 01:32:47,144
Use your power,
bring us together.

1413
01:32:47,771 --> 01:32:49,855
Guide us. Lead us.

1414
01:32:51,524 --> 01:32:54,318
Storm. Scott.

1415
01:32:56,488 --> 01:32:57,821
Jean.

1416
01:32:59,157 --> 01:33:01,325
Remember those names.

1417
01:33:02,327 --> 01:33:04,661
There are so many of us.

1418
01:33:05,330 --> 01:33:07,664
We will need you,
Professor.

1419
01:33:10,627 --> 01:33:13,045
I'll do my best.

1420
01:33:13,213 --> 01:33:14,880
Your best is enough.

1421
01:33:16,800 --> 01:33:18,509
Trust me.

1422
01:33:29,687 --> 01:33:31,522
(WIN D HOWLING)

1423
01:33:42,492 --> 01:33:44,952
There's 12 carriers
inbound, 10 miles!

1424
01:33:45,870 --> 01:33:46,954
They've found us.

1425
01:34:04,013 --> 01:34:06,140
REPORTER: Thousands of people
will be gathered here today.

1426
01:34:06,224 --> 01:34:07,641
They've come from
all over the world...

1427
01:34:07,725 --> 01:34:10,561
to witness history,
along with news crews...

1428
01:34:10,728 --> 01:34:12,229
from at least 50
different countries.

1429
01:34:13,940 --> 01:34:15,274
Thank you.

1430
01:34:16,526 --> 01:34:17,568
(BEEPS)

1431
01:34:17,694 --> 01:34:18,861
Can I see your
invitations, please?

1432
01:34:19,863 --> 01:34:21,113
Yes, you may.

1433
01:34:21,197 --> 01:34:22,322
These two are with me.

1434
01:34:22,407 --> 01:34:23,448
Go ahead.

1435
01:34:23,533 --> 01:34:24,658
Thank you.

1436
01:34:31,416 --> 01:34:32,791
CHARLES: Logan!

1437
01:34:32,917 --> 01:34:34,168
SECU RITY OFFICER:
Please, this way, sir.

1438
01:34:51,269 --> 01:34:53,353
(IN DISTINCT VOICES IN H EAD)

1439
01:35:01,279 --> 01:35:03,113
I haven't found her yet.
But she has to be here.

1440
01:35:03,281 --> 01:35:04,865
AN NOU NCER: The President
of the United States.

1441
01:35:05,200 --> 01:35:07,284
(PATRIOTIC MUSIC PLAYS)

1442
01:35:07,577 --> 01:35:09,286
(CROWD CH EERING)

1443
01:35:27,805 --> 01:35:29,514
My fellow Americans...

1444
01:35:29,682 --> 01:35:34,353
today we face the gravest
threat in our history...

1445
01:35:34,479 --> 01:35:35,646
mutants.

1446
01:35:35,730 --> 01:35:36,730
(VOICES RESUME)

1447
01:35:38,816 --> 01:35:41,235
We have prepared
for this threat.

1448
01:35:41,653 --> 01:35:43,862
(IN DISTINCT VOICES IN H EAD)

1449
01:35:44,239 --> 01:35:47,824
In the immortal words
of Robert Oppenheimer...

1450
01:35:47,992 --> 01:35:49,117
"Behold.

1451
01:35:49,702 --> 01:35:52,496
"The world will never be
the same again. "

1452
01:35:53,039 --> 01:35:55,123
(PATRIOTIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1453
01:35:58,336 --> 01:35:59,836
(CROWD CH EERING)

1454
01:36:12,058 --> 01:36:14,851
(COU NTRY MUSIC
PLAYING ON RADIO)

1455
01:36:23,027 --> 01:36:24,027
Can I help you?

1456
01:36:27,407 --> 01:36:28,615
No, you can't.

1457
01:36:28,950 --> 01:36:31,368
(STATIC)

1458
01:37:06,571 --> 01:37:07,821
Here they come.

1459
01:37:12,201 --> 01:37:13,660
(IN DISTINCT VOICES IN H EAD)

1460
01:37:14,579 --> 01:37:16,246
RAVEN: This is for you,
brothers and sisters.

1461
01:37:18,833 --> 01:37:19,916
Raven?

1462
01:37:22,670 --> 01:37:23,754
I have her.

1463
01:37:24,422 --> 01:37:25,630
(WITH RAVEN'S VOICE)
Let me go, Charles.

1464
01:37:27,800 --> 01:37:29,259
There. You see?

1465
01:37:29,427 --> 01:37:30,510
Secret Serviceman.

1466
01:37:30,678 --> 01:37:31,762
Left of the stage.

1467
01:37:31,888 --> 01:37:33,013
Got him.
CHARLES: Go.

1468
01:37:45,401 --> 01:37:47,319
(SENTIN ELS POWERING U P)

1469
01:37:53,785 --> 01:37:55,077
What the hell
are you doing?

1470
01:37:55,161 --> 01:37:56,578
I didn't tell you
to activate them.

1471
01:37:56,662 --> 01:37:57,829
I didn't.

1472
01:38:07,465 --> 01:38:09,383
(CROWD GASPING)

1473
01:38:16,432 --> 01:38:18,308
CHARLES: Raven, please, listen to me.

1474
01:38:18,810 --> 01:38:22,938
We've been given a second
chance to define who we are.

1475
01:38:24,982 --> 01:38:26,358
Don't do this.

1476
01:38:29,779 --> 01:38:32,030
Gentlemen, you cannot
pass this point.

1477
01:38:39,872 --> 01:38:41,623
We can't stop that many.

1478
01:38:41,791 --> 01:38:44,668
No, but we can
slow them down.

1479
01:38:59,434 --> 01:39:00,642
(CROWD CH EERING)

1480
01:39:11,028 --> 01:39:12,696
(SCREAMING)

1481
01:39:22,540 --> 01:39:24,207
Erik!

1482
01:39:27,211 --> 01:39:28,879
(SCREAMING CONTIN U ES)

1483
01:39:56,073 --> 01:39:57,657
(SCREAMING CONTIN U ES)

1484
01:39:58,493 --> 01:39:59,493
Ah!

1485
01:40:03,956 --> 01:40:05,290
(PANTING)

1486
01:40:09,045 --> 01:40:10,754
Storm!

1487
01:40:12,423 --> 01:40:13,632
(GROANS)

1488
01:40:15,843 --> 01:40:17,052
(SNARLS)

1489
01:40:23,768 --> 01:40:25,685
(YELLING)

1490
01:40:29,148 --> 01:40:30,565
Go, go, go!

1491
01:40:30,650 --> 01:40:31,942
(MEN CLAMORING)

1492
01:40:32,527 --> 01:40:33,610
MAN: Watch your head!

1493
01:40:34,070 --> 01:40:35,445
(SIRENS WAILING)

1494
01:40:46,582 --> 01:40:47,666
MAN 1: Go, go, go!

1495
01:40:47,750 --> 01:40:49,125
MAN 2: Take us to DEFCON 3.

1496
01:40:49,293 --> 01:40:50,460
Mr. President,
we are Code Red.

1497
01:40:50,586 --> 01:40:51,962
MAN 3: What's our air
defense readiness?

1498
01:40:52,129 --> 01:40:53,380
MAN 2: All our air
defenses are ready one.

1499
01:40:53,464 --> 01:40:54,881
N IXON: What the hell
happened out there?

1500
01:40:54,966 --> 01:40:56,049
I will fix it.

1501
01:40:56,133 --> 01:40:57,175
You said that before.

1502
01:40:57,301 --> 01:40:58,510
I wanted to
make a statement.

1503
01:40:58,636 --> 01:41:01,429
Now the whole goddamn world
knows we can't protect them.

1504
01:41:01,514 --> 01:41:02,597
TRASK: I will fix it.

1505
01:41:02,682 --> 01:41:04,474
N IXON:
You damn well better.

1506
01:41:37,466 --> 01:41:38,466
(GRU NTS)

1507
01:41:55,026 --> 01:41:57,068
(CROWD SCREAMING)

1508
01:42:15,921 --> 01:42:16,921
Charles!

1509
01:42:18,049 --> 01:42:19,382
No, no, no...
(GRU NTS)

1510
01:42:22,345 --> 01:42:23,511
(BOTH PANTING)

1511
01:42:29,560 --> 01:42:30,935
(FEMALE DISPATCH ER SPEAKING
OVER RADIO)

1512
01:42:31,354 --> 01:42:32,729
(SIRENS WAILING)

1513
01:42:58,923 --> 01:43:01,007
(BOTH PANTING)

1514
01:43:05,971 --> 01:43:07,722
STORM: Is everybody okay?

1515
01:43:10,935 --> 01:43:12,769
(GROANS SOFTLY)

1516
01:43:28,411 --> 01:43:29,577
(GASPS)

1517
01:43:41,590 --> 01:43:43,174
No!

1518
01:43:46,303 --> 01:43:47,345
Behind you.

1519
01:43:49,724 --> 01:43:51,599
Ah!

1520
01:43:53,018 --> 01:43:54,436
(GRU NTING)

1521
01:43:56,564 --> 01:43:58,523
(SCREAMING)

1522
01:44:32,016 --> 01:44:33,349
COLOSSUS: Now!

1523
01:44:35,311 --> 01:44:36,603
(SCREAMS)

1524
01:44:45,070 --> 01:44:46,362
(SU NSPOT SCREAMING)

1525
01:44:46,489 --> 01:44:47,572
(GROANS)

1526
01:44:56,707 --> 01:44:59,250
HAN K: I'm probably not supposed
to ask this kind of thing...

1527
01:44:59,752 --> 01:45:02,378
but in the future,
do I make it?

1528
01:45:02,838 --> 01:45:04,172
No.

1529
01:45:05,883 --> 01:45:07,300
But we can change that.

1530
01:45:07,384 --> 01:45:08,927
Right?

1531
01:45:13,682 --> 01:45:15,225
(ROARING)

1532
01:45:19,563 --> 01:45:21,189
Do what you were
made for.

1533
01:45:26,320 --> 01:45:27,320
(GRU NTS)

1534
01:45:30,407 --> 01:45:31,908
Where are you?

1535
01:45:37,706 --> 01:45:38,706
Ah!

1536
01:45:39,083 --> 01:45:40,124
(GROANS)

1537
01:45:45,589 --> 01:45:47,090
(ROARS)

1538
01:45:49,260 --> 01:45:50,760
I got this! Go!

1539
01:45:57,935 --> 01:45:58,935
(LOGAN COUGHS)

1540
01:46:14,827 --> 01:46:16,035
(GROAN ING)

1541
01:46:24,962 --> 01:46:26,629
(GRU NTING)

1542
01:46:33,470 --> 01:46:35,138
Oh, dear God, no.

1543
01:46:40,185 --> 01:46:41,686
(SCREAMING)

1544
01:46:51,030 --> 01:46:53,281
So much for being
a survivor.

1545
01:47:07,212 --> 01:47:08,880
(GASPING)

1546
01:47:23,395 --> 01:47:24,687
(GLASS CRACKING)

1547
01:47:25,022 --> 01:47:26,606
(ALARM RINGING)

1548
01:47:27,733 --> 01:47:29,901
(DETECTOR BEEPING)

1549
01:47:35,741 --> 01:47:37,033
One of them is in here.

1550
01:47:37,952 --> 01:47:39,285
(MEN SHOUTING)

1551
01:47:39,662 --> 01:47:41,412
TRASK: No, no, no!
Don't kill it!

1552
01:47:42,081 --> 01:47:43,164
I need it alive.

1553
01:47:44,041 --> 01:47:45,708
(RUMBLING)

1554
01:47:50,714 --> 01:47:51,881
(GRU NTING)

1555
01:47:56,595 --> 01:47:58,221
What the hell
has happened?

1556
01:48:07,731 --> 01:48:09,857
(METAL CREAKING)

1557
01:48:17,992 --> 01:48:19,117
(ALL GROAN ING)

1558
01:48:22,496 --> 01:48:23,746
(IN HALING)

1559
01:48:59,700 --> 01:49:00,867
(GROANS)

1560
01:49:05,998 --> 01:49:08,207
You built these
weapons to destroy us.

1561
01:49:09,168 --> 01:49:10,877
Why?

1562
01:49:14,465 --> 01:49:17,175
Because you are
afraid of our gifts.

1563
01:49:18,135 --> 01:49:20,636
Because we are different.

1564
01:49:21,805 --> 01:49:25,141
Humanity has always feared
that which is different.

1565
01:49:25,809 --> 01:49:27,185
Well, I am here
to tell you...

1566
01:49:27,394 --> 01:49:28,811
to tell the world...

1567
01:49:29,813 --> 01:49:31,981
you are right
to fear us.

1568
01:49:32,357 --> 01:49:34,067
We are the future.

1569
01:49:34,818 --> 01:49:37,487
We are the ones
who will inherit this earth.

1570
01:49:37,738 --> 01:49:40,323
And anyone who
stands in our way...

1571
01:49:40,491 --> 01:49:42,492
will suffer the same fate
as these men...

1572
01:49:42,659 --> 01:49:43,993
you see before you.

1573
01:49:51,210 --> 01:49:53,836
Today was meant to be
a display of your power.

1574
01:49:54,588 --> 01:49:56,672
Instead I give
you a glimpse...

1575
01:49:56,840 --> 01:50:00,343
of the devastation my race
can unleash upon yours.

1576
01:50:09,561 --> 01:50:11,729
Let this be a warning
to the world.

1577
01:50:12,439 --> 01:50:15,233
And to my mutant brothers
and sisters out there...

1578
01:50:16,026 --> 01:50:17,443
I say this.

1579
01:50:18,195 --> 01:50:19,862
No more hiding.

1580
01:50:20,030 --> 01:50:21,864
No more suffering.

1581
01:50:22,699 --> 01:50:25,076
You have lived
in the shadows...

1582
01:50:25,244 --> 01:50:28,079
in shame and fear for
too long. Come out.

1583
01:50:29,331 --> 01:50:30,665
Join me.

1584
01:50:30,749 --> 01:50:34,252
Fight together in
a brotherhood of our kind.

1585
01:50:34,878 --> 01:50:36,546
A new tomorrow...

1586
01:50:37,756 --> 01:50:39,549
that starts today.

1587
01:50:43,929 --> 01:50:45,221
(GROANS)

1588
01:50:46,765 --> 01:50:48,599
MAGN ETO:
All those years wasted...

1589
01:50:48,767 --> 01:50:50,768
fighting each other,
Charles.

1590
01:50:54,314 --> 01:50:57,942
To have a precious
few of them back...

1591
01:51:06,076 --> 01:51:07,994
(RUMBLING)

1592
01:51:12,374 --> 01:51:13,875
(BANGING)

1593
01:51:32,686 --> 01:51:33,895
(GROANS)

1594
01:51:36,690 --> 01:51:37,899
MAN: Mr. President, sir.
Stand down.

1595
01:51:37,983 --> 01:51:39,859
I said, stand down!

1596
01:51:41,695 --> 01:51:43,362
You want to make
a statement?

1597
01:51:43,822 --> 01:51:45,615
Kill me. Fine.

1598
01:51:45,782 --> 01:51:47,700
But spare
everyone else.

1599
01:51:59,087 --> 01:52:00,254
(GRU NTING)

1600
01:52:00,339 --> 01:52:02,340
Very heroic,
Mr. President...

1601
01:52:02,841 --> 01:52:04,342
but you had no intention...

1602
01:52:04,468 --> 01:52:06,677
of sparing any of us.

1603
01:52:07,137 --> 01:52:10,473
The future of our
species begins now.

1604
01:52:10,557 --> 01:52:11,641
(GU NS COCKING)

1605
01:52:18,732 --> 01:52:19,815
(BEEPING)

1606
01:52:35,916 --> 01:52:37,250
(GASPING)

1607
01:52:46,009 --> 01:52:47,176
You used to be
a better shot.

1608
01:52:47,261 --> 01:52:48,511
Trust me,
I still am.

1609
01:53:02,359 --> 01:53:03,859
Get out of my head,
Charles!

1610
01:53:04,027 --> 01:53:05,528
Raven.

1611
01:53:05,696 --> 01:53:07,571
Please, do not make us
the enemy today.

1612
01:53:07,781 --> 01:53:09,615
Look around you.
We already are.

1613
01:53:10,117 --> 01:53:11,867
(BREATH ING H EAVILY)
CHARLES: Not all of us.

1614
01:53:12,077 --> 01:53:14,328
All you've done so far...

1615
01:53:14,663 --> 01:53:16,664
is save the lives
of these men.

1616
01:53:17,708 --> 01:53:20,251
You can show them
a better path.

1617
01:53:23,922 --> 01:53:25,381
Shut her down, Charles.

1618
01:53:27,592 --> 01:53:31,220
I've been trying to control
you ever since the day we met...

1619
01:53:31,596 --> 01:53:33,597
and look where
that's got us.

1620
01:53:35,726 --> 01:53:38,561
Everything that happens now...

1621
01:53:39,229 --> 01:53:41,397
is in your hands.

1622
01:53:42,024 --> 01:53:44,108
(BREATH ING DEEPLY)

1623
01:53:45,444 --> 01:53:48,237
I have faith in you,
Raven.

1624
01:54:02,461 --> 01:54:03,961
(SCREAMING)

1625
01:55:05,857 --> 01:55:07,108
(EXHALES)

1626
01:55:14,074 --> 01:55:16,492
(IN DISTINCT MU RMU RING)

1627
01:55:26,920 --> 01:55:29,046
RAVEN: He's all
yours, Charles.

1628
01:55:43,854 --> 01:55:44,854
(GRU NTS)

1629
01:55:56,616 --> 01:55:59,243
If you let them have me,
I'm as good as dead.

1630
01:55:59,411 --> 01:56:00,786
You know that.

1631
01:56:01,455 --> 01:56:03,038
I know.

1632
01:56:05,041 --> 01:56:06,709
Goodbye, old friend.

1633
01:56:09,379 --> 01:56:11,213
Goodbye, Erik.

1634
01:56:29,774 --> 01:56:31,442
(H ELICOPTER HOVERING)

1635
01:56:41,077 --> 01:56:42,411
(SIGHS)

1636
01:56:44,623 --> 01:56:46,624
HAN K: Are you sure you
should let them go?

1637
01:56:47,584 --> 01:56:48,959
CHARLES: Yes.

1638
01:56:49,586 --> 01:56:51,295
I have hope for them.

1639
01:56:52,464 --> 01:56:56,467
There's going to be a time,
Hank, when we are all together.

1640
01:57:00,347 --> 01:57:02,306
HAN K: What about Logan?

1641
01:57:08,271 --> 01:57:11,023
(SOFT '70s SONG PLAYING)

1642
01:57:34,130 --> 01:57:36,799
The first time

1643
01:57:37,759 --> 01:57:38,968
(GROANS)

1644
01:57:39,803 --> 01:57:45,057
Ever I saw your face

1645
01:57:50,021 --> 01:57:53,357
I thought the sun...

1646
01:57:53,441 --> 01:57:54,483
(BELL RINGING)

1647
01:58:17,924 --> 01:58:21,176
KITTY: Buckminster Fuller is a
great example of an architect...

1648
01:58:21,261 --> 01:58:25,514
whose ideas were very similar
to those of a utopian future.

1649
01:58:31,855 --> 01:58:34,523
Good morning, Logan.
Late start. (CH UCKLES)

1650
01:58:40,780 --> 01:58:42,448
(IN DISTINCT CONVERSATIONS)

1651
01:58:44,618 --> 01:58:45,951
Have a good lunch.

1652
01:58:46,119 --> 01:58:47,369
Good job.
STU DENT: Thank you.

1653
01:58:47,704 --> 01:58:49,038
STORM: Very good job.

1654
01:58:49,914 --> 01:58:51,498
LOGAN: Storm.

1655
01:59:22,572 --> 01:59:23,656
Jean.

1656
01:59:25,075 --> 01:59:26,408
Hey, Logan.

1657
01:59:26,951 --> 01:59:28,077
Jean.

1658
01:59:28,787 --> 01:59:30,496
Are you okay?

1659
01:59:32,248 --> 01:59:33,666
You're here.

1660
01:59:34,292 --> 01:59:36,335
Where else would I be?

1661
01:59:38,630 --> 01:59:39,630
Whoa.

1662
01:59:40,465 --> 01:59:42,424
Easy, pal.

1663
01:59:42,550 --> 01:59:43,634
(CH UCKLES)

1664
01:59:43,968 --> 01:59:46,512
Well, some things
never change.

1665
01:59:47,931 --> 01:59:49,515
It's good to
see you, Scott.

1666
01:59:51,309 --> 01:59:52,559
Uh-huh.

1667
01:59:52,644 --> 01:59:53,811
See you
later, Jean.

1668
01:59:57,941 --> 01:59:59,483
Professor.

1669
01:59:59,943 --> 02:00:02,736
Logan, is everything
all right?

1670
02:00:06,116 --> 02:00:07,574
Yeah.

1671
02:00:08,618 --> 02:00:10,452
Yeah, I think it is.

1672
02:00:27,011 --> 02:00:28,220
You did it.

1673
02:00:28,304 --> 02:00:29,555
Did what?

1674
02:00:29,639 --> 02:00:31,640
Logan, don't you have
a class to teach?

1675
02:00:32,308 --> 02:00:33,976
A class to teach?

1676
02:00:35,019 --> 02:00:36,103
History.

1677
02:00:36,813 --> 02:00:38,313
History?

1678
02:00:39,149 --> 02:00:40,816
Actually, I could use
some help with that.

1679
02:00:41,317 --> 02:00:42,818
Help with what?

1680
02:00:42,986 --> 02:00:46,488
Pretty much
everything after 1973.

1681
02:00:51,035 --> 02:00:54,079
I think the history I
know is a little different.

1682
02:00:55,707 --> 02:00:57,416
Welcome back.

1683
02:01:00,170 --> 02:01:01,837
It's good to
see you, Charles.

1684
02:01:03,214 --> 02:01:05,048
It's good to see everyone.

1685
02:01:05,216 --> 02:01:06,717
Well...

1686
02:01:07,343 --> 02:01:09,511
I had a promise to keep.

1687
02:01:10,680 --> 02:01:13,932
You and I have a lot of
catching up to do.

1688
02:01:14,851 --> 02:01:16,351
Yeah.

1689
02:01:19,898 --> 02:01:22,024
What's the last thing
you remember?

1690
02:01:27,113 --> 02:01:28,864
Drowning.

1691
02:01:37,123 --> 02:01:38,373
CHARLES: The past.

1692
02:01:39,876 --> 02:01:41,126
A new...

1693
02:01:41,211 --> 02:01:42,961
and uncertain world.

1694
02:01:54,390 --> 02:01:56,683
CHARLES: A world of
endless possibilities.

1695
02:01:59,437 --> 02:02:01,563
And infinite outcomes.

1696
02:02:03,233 --> 02:02:04,358
You kidding me?

1697
02:02:04,484 --> 02:02:05,943
Oh, he's alive!

1698
02:02:07,779 --> 02:02:09,571
(COUGHS)

1699
02:02:10,323 --> 02:02:13,075
CHARLES: Countless
choices define our fate.

1700
02:02:13,993 --> 02:02:16,453
Each choice,
each moment...

1701
02:02:16,621 --> 02:02:19,248
a ripple in the river of time.

1702
02:02:19,415 --> 02:02:21,750
What do you want us to do
with him, Major Stryker?

1703
02:02:21,918 --> 02:02:23,669
CHARLES: Enough ripples...

1704
02:02:23,837 --> 02:02:26,421
and you change the tide.

1705
02:02:26,589 --> 02:02:27,673
I'll take him from here.

1706
02:02:27,841 --> 02:02:31,760
CHARLES: For the future
is never truly set.

1707
02:10:34,577 --> 02:10:38,413
(CROWD CHANTING
IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE)

